1
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,768
Here are the voting results.

2
00:00:08,204 --> 00:00:09,471
The voting results.

3
00:00:10,173 --> 00:00:11,106
I'm so nervous.

4
00:00:12,375 --> 00:00:15,344
With 11 votes...

5
00:00:16,247 --> 00:00:18,547
to two votes,

6
00:00:18,548 --> 00:00:19,849
(11 votes vs 2 votes)

7
00:00:20,383 --> 00:00:22,818
the new leader
of the Community House is...

8
00:00:24,854 --> 00:00:25,720
No way.

9
00:00:26,523 --> 00:00:27,790
Incredible.

10
00:00:32,495 --> 00:00:34,663
(Three hours earlier)

11
00:00:34,664 --> 00:00:36,665
Please vote for me. Thank you.

12
00:00:37,901 --> 00:00:38,767
Impressive.

13
00:00:38,768 --> 00:00:41,203
(The final speeches end.)

14
00:00:41,283 --> 00:00:42,216
(Voting begins in two hours.)

15
00:00:42,238 --> 00:00:43,939
- That was great.
- Good work.

16
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:45,241
You did great.

17
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:49,911
Superman's strategy today was
something else.

18
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:54,015
The way he delivered his speech made
it seem like he'd done that kind of work.

19
00:00:54,016 --> 00:00:55,216
I think he is strategic.

20
00:00:55,217 --> 00:00:56,818
He's no joke.

21
00:00:57,120 --> 00:01:00,255
He knows how to win people over.

22
00:01:00,256 --> 00:01:01,290
That's right.

23
00:01:01,391 --> 00:01:02,524
Good work.

24
00:01:02,525 --> 00:01:04,526
I think you crushed me.

25
00:01:04,527 --> 00:01:06,695
- Have you ever campaigned before?
- No, I haven't.

26
00:01:06,996 --> 00:01:08,196
I've done it a lot.

27
00:01:08,197 --> 00:01:09,898
- Your experience shows.
- Of course.

28
00:01:10,133 --> 00:01:11,700
Polar Bear is just...

29
00:01:11,701 --> 00:01:15,170
I bet she'll run for president
in about ten years.

30
00:01:15,171 --> 00:01:16,371
- No, I won't.
- I'm serious.

31
00:01:16,707 --> 00:01:17,740
She'll do great things.

32
00:01:17,741 --> 00:01:19,508
To me, doesn't this seem...

33
00:01:19,509 --> 00:01:21,076
like bipartisan unity at this point?

34
00:01:21,945 --> 00:01:23,712
I'm losing it. This is so hard.

35
00:01:23,713 --> 00:01:25,848
I'm really torn right now.

36
00:01:26,149 --> 00:01:28,784
(Smoking area)

37
00:01:28,785 --> 00:01:30,085
Polar Bear will go far.

38
00:01:30,086 --> 00:01:34,022
I really relate to Polar Bear too,
but first...

39
00:01:34,023 --> 00:01:35,891
- Feasibility.
- A realistic plan?

40
00:01:36,226 --> 00:01:38,160
- It matters.
- It's reality versus ideals.

41
00:01:38,261 --> 00:01:39,127
Right.

42
00:01:39,128 --> 00:01:40,929
Superman clearly believes...

43
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:43,899
not everyone will survive until the end.

44
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:45,300
- He's sure of it.
- Right.

45
00:01:45,301 --> 00:01:47,069
- It's realistic.
- He has experience.

46
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:49,705
- When administrations change in the US,
- Right.

47
00:01:49,706 --> 00:01:53,542
most Americans don't focus
on people with expert knowledge.

48
00:01:53,710 --> 00:01:56,680
Most care about making ends meet.

49
00:01:56,681 --> 00:01:58,480
- Right.
- They focus on immediate concerns.

50
00:01:58,481 --> 00:02:00,817
- That's what changes how they vote.
- Right.

51
00:02:00,818 --> 00:02:03,420
Superman's strategy today was
a Trump speech.

52
00:02:03,421 --> 00:02:05,754
Right, it was a Trump speech.

53
00:02:05,855 --> 00:02:07,690
But what he did at the end,

54
00:02:07,691 --> 00:02:09,991
addressing each person, was moving
and clever.

55
00:02:10,527 --> 00:02:12,295
That was one of the highlights.

56
00:02:12,296 --> 00:02:13,662
- It was.
- A true highlight.

57
00:02:13,663 --> 00:02:15,831
Our Go Ae Shin, Director Go's...

58
00:02:15,832 --> 00:02:17,466
leadership and self-sacrifice.

59
00:02:17,467 --> 00:02:20,102
(Superman moved them
by naming every resident.)

60
00:02:20,103 --> 00:02:23,072
Ted is like our mediator.

61
00:02:23,073 --> 00:02:24,373
He's our usual host.

62
00:02:24,374 --> 00:02:26,109
He's also so seasoned.

63
00:02:26,110 --> 00:02:27,743
He's so composed.

64
00:02:28,678 --> 00:02:30,045
I think I got crushed.

65
00:02:31,147 --> 00:02:33,715
I don't think we can convince...

66
00:02:33,716 --> 00:02:36,318
anyone firmly against voting for you.

67
00:02:36,319 --> 00:02:38,453
We should identify potential voters...

68
00:02:38,955 --> 00:02:40,589
- and win them over in two hours.
- Right.

69
00:02:42,292 --> 00:02:44,360
Nangja.

70
00:02:44,861 --> 00:02:46,361
- I'm counting on you.
- For what?

71
00:02:46,362 --> 00:02:47,329
Your vote.

72
00:02:49,232 --> 00:02:50,432
Need some help, Banu?

73
00:02:51,835 --> 00:02:53,169
Have you decided, Banu?

74
00:02:54,070 --> 00:02:55,070
Still thinking?

75
00:02:56,172 --> 00:02:57,205
Vote for me.

76
00:02:58,808 --> 00:03:01,543
- The speeches gave me a lot to consider.
- Me too.

77
00:03:01,544 --> 00:03:04,246
I'll say this later
when everyone's together.

78
00:03:04,247 --> 00:03:05,881
But we can't rule this out.

79
00:03:06,149 --> 00:03:09,619
The leader can secretly go back...

80
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,919
on the new rules.

81
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:13,589
Once a leader is registered,
the pledges submitted...

82
00:03:13,590 --> 00:03:16,692
may be freely deleted.

83
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:21,730
(The leader's pledges may be
empty promises.)

84
00:03:22,298 --> 00:03:25,166
Presidential candidates say...

85
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:28,069
anything to get elected.

86
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:30,538
I wasn't really swayed by them.

87
00:03:30,539 --> 00:03:33,308
- Me neither.
- I wanted to see who sounded sincere...

88
00:03:34,077 --> 00:03:36,745
and who could actually move me.

89
00:03:37,113 --> 00:03:40,249
- Right.
- They were both just saying...

90
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:41,750
whatever voters wanted to hear.

91
00:03:41,751 --> 00:03:43,385
Right. They're about even.

92
00:03:43,386 --> 00:03:45,387
I think everything else is bull.

93
00:03:45,755 --> 00:03:46,621
It's just...

94
00:03:48,224 --> 00:03:49,324
He called it bull.

95
00:03:49,726 --> 00:03:51,460
I see it very differently.

96
00:03:51,461 --> 00:03:53,462
Being skilled with words...

97
00:03:53,463 --> 00:03:55,664
and who someone really is
are two different things.

98
00:03:55,865 --> 00:03:58,333
For example, the way Dark Knight
solves problems is...

99
00:03:58,334 --> 00:03:59,534
very different.

100
00:03:59,535 --> 00:04:01,036
When he persuaded Michael,

101
00:04:01,037 --> 00:04:02,737
everyone was explaining it logically.

102
00:04:02,738 --> 00:04:05,740
Then he said, "Michael, you trust me.
Do it."

103
00:04:06,042 --> 00:04:07,009
Things like that.

104
00:04:08,077 --> 00:04:10,679
I think that's also very important.

105
00:04:10,813 --> 00:04:12,313
And in life,

106
00:04:12,616 --> 00:04:15,384
I don't think logic alone gets you far.

107
00:04:15,551 --> 00:04:17,753
You could simply act like Go Ae Shin.

108
00:04:17,954 --> 00:04:19,421
I really like that side of her too.

109
00:04:19,722 --> 00:04:22,457
I'd have liked to see
that kind of leader too.

110
00:04:23,226 --> 00:04:25,194
Today's main concern is...

111
00:04:25,195 --> 00:04:28,597
that today is the last day
to use four attack tokens.

112
00:04:28,765 --> 00:04:30,866
There could be another bloodbath.

113
00:04:30,867 --> 00:04:33,335
- Right.
- So let's discuss that first.

114
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:35,137
Can you go tell them?

115
00:04:35,138 --> 00:04:36,505
- Sure.
- Can you do it?

116
00:04:36,506 --> 00:04:38,274
- I...
- Then I'll back you up.

117
00:04:38,275 --> 00:04:39,475
Okay, let's go.

118
00:04:40,176 --> 00:04:44,646
- There's something I'd like to discuss.
- Okay.

119
00:04:44,948 --> 00:04:46,782
First, today is...

120
00:04:46,783 --> 00:04:49,251
the spy's last day to attack.

121
00:04:49,953 --> 00:04:52,354
I think those under suspicion should...

122
00:04:52,355 --> 00:04:54,323
be the first to receive...

123
00:04:54,324 --> 00:04:56,225
favorability votes and ideology checks.

124
00:04:56,359 --> 00:04:58,860
Put the suspects first in line.

125
00:04:59,162 --> 00:05:00,095
Suspects?

126
00:05:00,096 --> 00:05:02,964
I mean, suspected spies.

127
00:05:02,965 --> 00:05:05,167
Should we choose the spy suspects?

128
00:05:05,168 --> 00:05:06,034
Who the spy might be?

129
00:05:06,035 --> 00:05:07,869
Yes, and I'm asking...

130
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:11,806
whoever is elected leader today
to take on that role.

131
00:05:12,041 --> 00:05:15,043
That will be my most important criterion.

132
00:05:15,044 --> 00:05:16,744
You'll vote for whoever will do that?

133
00:05:16,745 --> 00:05:18,813
I want someone to organize a system...

134
00:05:18,814 --> 00:05:20,682
that keeps everyone safe.

135
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:22,083
Putting that in place is...

136
00:05:22,084 --> 00:05:24,286
one thing I want...

137
00:05:24,287 --> 00:05:26,154
from whoever becomes Lifetime Leader.

138
00:05:26,155 --> 00:05:29,190
That mattered to me
when drafting my pledges too.

139
00:05:29,359 --> 00:05:30,492
Punitive taxation.

140
00:05:30,727 --> 00:05:31,860
As I said earlier.

141
00:05:33,096 --> 00:05:35,064
We have a communal fund.

142
00:05:35,065 --> 00:05:39,134
But the leader can directly impose it
on a traitor or spy.

143
00:05:39,135 --> 00:05:41,804
It's almost their only power to punish.

144
00:05:41,805 --> 00:05:43,338
If someone gets greedy,

145
00:05:43,673 --> 00:05:45,474
breaks our agreement, takes everyone out,

146
00:05:45,475 --> 00:05:46,642
and steals all their money,

147
00:05:46,643 --> 00:05:49,177
emboldened by being the traitor,

148
00:05:49,512 --> 00:05:51,513
and just wants to hold out until the end,

149
00:05:51,748 --> 00:05:53,816
I believe we should impose
punitive taxes on them.

150
00:05:54,017 --> 00:05:55,150
Make it 100 percent.

151
00:05:55,151 --> 00:05:56,386
With punitive taxes,

152
00:05:56,387 --> 00:05:58,354
- they won't dare?
- Yes, punitive taxes.

153
00:05:59,422 --> 00:06:03,258
But for Superman's punitive taxes
to be meaningful,

154
00:06:03,259 --> 00:06:05,894
we must first confirm as a fact...

155
00:06:05,895 --> 00:06:08,063
that the person being taxed...

156
00:06:08,064 --> 00:06:09,898
is definitely the spy.

157
00:06:09,899 --> 00:06:12,167
Without that certainty,
punitive taxation could...

158
00:06:12,168 --> 00:06:14,703
create innocent victims instead.

159
00:06:14,704 --> 00:06:17,205
That concerned me a little.

160
00:06:17,206 --> 00:06:19,474
I said I'd run a situation room...

161
00:06:19,475 --> 00:06:22,411
because before discussing punishment...

162
00:06:22,412 --> 00:06:23,912
for someone identified as the spy,

163
00:06:23,913 --> 00:06:25,347
we need to consider...

164
00:06:25,348 --> 00:06:27,582
that taxation might not threaten the spy.

165
00:06:27,583 --> 00:06:30,852
We can't rule out that possibility.

166
00:06:30,853 --> 00:06:32,854
- Because...
- We should...

167
00:06:32,855 --> 00:06:35,624
narrow down the spy's identity first.

168
00:06:35,825 --> 00:06:37,926
Simply saying we'll tax the spy doesn't...

169
00:06:37,927 --> 00:06:40,962
seem very meaningful
in our current situation.

170
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,934
I need to use the restroom first.

171
00:06:46,169 --> 00:06:47,369
I've been holding it in.

172
00:06:47,469 --> 00:06:49,704
- Ten-minute restroom break?
- Let's take one.

173
00:06:56,479 --> 00:06:58,480
Now that the candidates are gone,

174
00:06:58,915 --> 00:07:01,049
why don't we talk freely...

175
00:07:01,050 --> 00:07:02,985
about what we think of them?

176
00:07:02,986 --> 00:07:06,221
I like them both,
and I'm still weighing my options.

177
00:07:06,222 --> 00:07:07,623
I'm still weighing them.

178
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:09,857
Me too. I really don't know.

179
00:07:10,426 --> 00:07:11,326
Me neither.

180
00:07:11,327 --> 00:07:14,396
I lean one way and then the other.

181
00:07:14,397 --> 00:07:16,598
I keep going back and forth.

182
00:07:16,599 --> 00:07:19,302
But in terms of leadership...

183
00:07:19,303 --> 00:07:22,871
and trustworthiness,
there isn't much difference.

184
00:07:22,872 --> 00:07:26,241
They'd both listen to our opinions.

185
00:07:27,009 --> 00:07:28,376
That's why I'm so torn.

186
00:07:33,049 --> 00:07:34,116
(Tensions Under the Roof)

187
00:07:34,584 --> 00:07:36,351
(The Community)

188
00:07:36,352 --> 00:07:37,385
(An announcement begins.)

189
00:07:37,386 --> 00:07:40,622
(The Weight of the Crown)

190
00:07:42,459 --> 00:07:45,194
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

191
00:07:46,929 --> 00:07:50,298
The Lifetime Leader election will
now begin.

192
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:51,633
Please vote for me.

193
00:07:52,401 --> 00:07:56,405
- You have 30 minutes to vote.
- That's short.

194
00:07:56,406 --> 00:07:57,739
- They're quick.
- First again?

195
00:07:58,217 --> 00:08:01,819
Residents, please visit
the Community Center...

196
00:08:01,844 --> 00:08:04,012
and cast your votes.

197
00:08:06,315 --> 00:08:07,482
I'm going.

198
00:08:07,483 --> 00:08:08,349
I'll go now.

199
00:08:08,517 --> 00:08:11,219
(Voting begins.)

200
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:17,125
(The Community Center)

201
00:08:17,994 --> 00:08:20,529
(The Community, Polar Bear, Superman)

202
00:08:27,170 --> 00:08:28,437
I'm submitting my vote.

203
00:08:28,438 --> 00:08:31,039
(Hippo, Nangja, and Dark Knight
quickly finish voting.)

204
00:08:31,808 --> 00:08:33,342
Here's what I'm wondering.

205
00:08:33,743 --> 00:08:35,711
There are 13 of us now.

206
00:08:35,978 --> 00:08:38,079
The vote could be seven to six.

207
00:08:38,214 --> 00:08:40,215
What if someone who didn't vote...

208
00:08:40,216 --> 00:08:42,884
for the winning candidate has
to evict someone?

209
00:08:42,885 --> 00:08:44,986
Don't you think that could happen?

210
00:08:44,987 --> 00:08:46,988
Right. Something unexpected happened...

211
00:08:46,989 --> 00:08:49,324
after our Korean-Chinese debate.

212
00:08:49,792 --> 00:08:53,528
The people who voted...

213
00:08:53,529 --> 00:08:55,296
in favor of it never expected
to be charged...

214
00:08:55,297 --> 00:08:56,865
a thousand dollars each the next day.

215
00:08:57,467 --> 00:09:00,135
But that's what happened.

216
00:09:04,207 --> 00:09:06,842
Here's what I was thinking.

217
00:09:08,344 --> 00:09:12,280
If it came down to the majority...

218
00:09:12,281 --> 00:09:14,582
and the minority...

219
00:09:15,318 --> 00:09:18,420
and the minority had to do something...

220
00:09:18,421 --> 00:09:19,588
I thought so too.

221
00:09:19,956 --> 00:09:22,591
It could say, "Choose one person
from the minority."

222
00:09:22,592 --> 00:09:24,126
That could happen.

223
00:09:24,127 --> 00:09:26,328
- I think that's very possible.
- Right.

224
00:09:26,796 --> 00:09:28,296
But if that happens...

225
00:09:28,898 --> 00:09:32,834
and most people vote for Superman,

226
00:09:32,835 --> 00:09:35,670
if I vote for Polar Bear
and end up in the minority,

227
00:09:35,671 --> 00:09:36,771
they might abandon me.

228
00:09:36,772 --> 00:09:38,139
- But think about this.
- But...

229
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:39,841
if most vote for Polar Bear...

230
00:09:39,842 --> 00:09:41,309
and I vote for Superman,

231
00:09:41,310 --> 00:09:42,644
putting me in the minority,

232
00:09:42,879 --> 00:09:44,312
- Polar Bear would save me.
- Yes.

233
00:09:44,747 --> 00:09:45,680
Know what I mean?

234
00:09:45,681 --> 00:09:48,216
So if I vote for Superman,

235
00:09:48,451 --> 00:09:50,419
I'll survive in the majority...

236
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:52,087
and in the minority.

237
00:09:52,088 --> 00:09:54,556
I've always thought Superman was...

238
00:09:54,557 --> 00:09:56,057
- I favored him too.
- decisive.

239
00:09:56,058 --> 00:09:57,459
But we must think about this.

240
00:09:58,060 --> 00:09:59,127
If that happens,

241
00:09:59,763 --> 00:10:02,931
this will become Superman's Community.

242
00:10:02,932 --> 00:10:05,634
So there won't be room for us.

243
00:10:07,370 --> 00:10:08,337
We must consider that.

244
00:10:09,039 --> 00:10:10,305
I'm thinking long-term.

245
00:10:10,306 --> 00:10:11,573
I have a point.

246
00:10:12,174 --> 00:10:13,941
What do I do?

247
00:10:14,844 --> 00:10:16,044
Have you decided?

248
00:10:16,279 --> 00:10:17,212
I'm so torn.

249
00:10:18,147 --> 00:10:20,148
Ted, hurry up and decide.

250
00:10:20,349 --> 00:10:21,984
- It's hard.
- Join me. I'll be good.

251
00:10:21,985 --> 00:10:23,051
It's hard.

252
00:10:23,252 --> 00:10:25,320
I'm listening. My ears are open.

253
00:10:26,522 --> 00:10:27,655
This is hard.

254
00:10:29,225 --> 00:10:30,626
Next. Did you vote?

255
00:10:30,627 --> 00:10:32,494
Anyone who hasn't voted yet...

256
00:10:32,828 --> 00:10:34,462
Banu, want to go vote?

257
00:10:52,682 --> 00:10:56,718
(Banu, Sugar, Benjamin, Michael,
and Gray finish voting.)

258
00:10:57,253 --> 00:10:59,387
I think Superman is a little more...

259
00:11:00,022 --> 00:11:01,422
I originally thought...

260
00:11:01,557 --> 00:11:04,026
that if we only cared about peace,
coexistence,

261
00:11:04,027 --> 00:11:06,794
and beautiful ideals,
Polar Bear would be right.

262
00:11:07,196 --> 00:11:09,030
So far, we've all been willing...

263
00:11:09,031 --> 00:11:10,665
to make reasonable sacrifices...

264
00:11:10,666 --> 00:11:13,268
to help someone else.

265
00:11:13,436 --> 00:11:16,037
But say I have assets
I worked my whole life to build.

266
00:11:16,339 --> 00:11:19,607
Someone next to me is sick and dying.

267
00:11:19,709 --> 00:11:22,910
It makes no sense to give them...

268
00:11:22,911 --> 00:11:25,646
all of my life's assets just to save them.

269
00:11:25,647 --> 00:11:27,348
- It's hard.
- They aren't family.

270
00:11:27,627 --> 00:11:30,252
Even in that situation,
what would Polar Bear do?

271
00:11:30,253 --> 00:11:32,587
She said she'd still save that person.

272
00:11:32,588 --> 00:11:35,991
That means Polar Bear wouldn't save them
with her personal funds.

273
00:11:35,992 --> 00:11:38,093
Saving them would be our collective duty.

274
00:11:38,094 --> 00:11:40,795
Honestly, I don't want...

275
00:11:40,796 --> 00:11:42,931
to be forced to sacrifice that much.

276
00:11:43,332 --> 00:11:44,766
If I'm forced to do it...

277
00:11:44,767 --> 00:11:47,001
and I say no,

278
00:11:47,303 --> 00:11:48,970
I'll become the villain.

279
00:11:49,404 --> 00:11:52,006
When I think about that,

280
00:11:52,007 --> 00:11:55,176
Superman seems like someone
who could firmly say no.

281
00:11:55,177 --> 00:11:57,345
That's what I thought.

282
00:12:04,286 --> 00:12:05,586
Michael, what will happen next?

283
00:12:06,402 --> 00:12:07,969
I think...

284
00:12:08,491 --> 00:12:10,225
a nuclear bomb will go off soon.

285
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:11,993
Exactly. That's why...

286
00:12:12,428 --> 00:12:14,396
- I just thought of something.
- What?

287
00:12:15,331 --> 00:12:18,000
They'll test the leader immediately.

288
00:12:18,001 --> 00:12:19,768
Right. They'll test their ability.

289
00:12:20,102 --> 00:12:21,736
Someone may be evicted today.

290
00:12:21,737 --> 00:12:23,438
It may not be one person.

291
00:12:24,306 --> 00:12:25,606
It could be four.

292
00:12:25,841 --> 00:12:26,641
Four people?

293
00:12:27,576 --> 00:12:29,410
What if the spy stops caring?

294
00:12:29,845 --> 00:12:33,047
They could use every code check
and kill everyone.

295
00:12:36,285 --> 00:12:37,252
Who did you choose?

296
00:12:41,290 --> 00:12:43,658
I just don't want to be in the minority.

297
00:12:43,659 --> 00:12:45,526
- So I chose the larger group.
- Okay.

298
00:12:45,527 --> 00:12:46,794
- That's why I'm checking.
- Right.

299
00:12:49,532 --> 00:12:51,133
Has everyone voted but us two?

300
00:12:51,134 --> 00:12:52,033
Ted.

301
00:12:52,835 --> 00:12:54,469
- Shall we go?
- Let's go together.

302
00:12:55,438 --> 00:12:56,304
Going together?

303
00:12:56,739 --> 00:12:58,140
- Ted hasn't voted?
- Not yet.

304
00:12:58,141 --> 00:13:00,108
- Everyone else voted?
- Let's go together.

305
00:13:00,109 --> 00:13:02,110
- Good luck.
- Let's do this.

306
00:13:02,445 --> 00:13:04,047
This is driving me crazy.

307
00:13:07,183 --> 00:13:08,049
Are there many votes?

308
00:13:08,784 --> 00:13:10,217
There's no way to know...

309
00:13:10,278 --> 00:13:14,348
because what people tell me
and what they do are very different.

310
00:13:14,857 --> 00:13:15,723
Seriously.

311
00:13:16,524 --> 00:13:19,060
- It's the same for me.
- Because for someone,

312
00:13:19,061 --> 00:13:19,994
I saw them tell...

313
00:13:20,329 --> 00:13:21,863
you they'd vote for you...

314
00:13:21,864 --> 00:13:23,531
then tell her they'd vote for her.

315
00:13:27,803 --> 00:13:31,439
I almost chose Polar Bear
because her ideals match mine.

316
00:13:31,841 --> 00:13:33,310
I also thought following
his leadership might...

317
00:13:33,311 --> 00:13:35,243
be worthwhile
because it differs from mine.

318
00:13:35,911 --> 00:13:36,978
But then,

319
00:13:38,381 --> 00:13:39,480
one pledge was...

320
00:13:39,782 --> 00:13:44,052
to tax anyone who tried
to break away from the group.

321
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:45,053
That bothers you.

322
00:13:45,922 --> 00:13:47,622
The spy is our common enemy.

323
00:13:47,623 --> 00:13:48,456
Right.

324
00:13:48,457 --> 00:13:49,558
If someone breaks away...

325
00:13:49,559 --> 00:13:51,993
or agrees to act selfishly,

326
00:13:52,328 --> 00:13:54,996
they may face social censure,
but do they deserve punishment?

327
00:13:55,397 --> 00:13:58,199
Should the leader demand all their money?

328
00:13:58,267 --> 00:14:00,736
It violently suppresses autonomy.

329
00:14:00,737 --> 00:14:01,636
That's my concern.

330
00:14:01,637 --> 00:14:02,737
In that situation,

331
00:14:02,738 --> 00:14:04,441
the leader could be mistaken.

332
00:14:04,442 --> 00:14:06,040
It may or may not be betrayal.

333
00:14:06,308 --> 00:14:08,576
I'm worried about an error in judgment.

334
00:14:09,011 --> 00:14:10,444
An innocent person could suffer.

335
00:14:10,579 --> 00:14:12,346
That's the one thing bothering me.

336
00:14:12,347 --> 00:14:13,482
But it looked like...

337
00:14:13,483 --> 00:14:14,815
Hippo and Sugar were...

338
00:14:14,816 --> 00:14:16,918
- leaning toward Superman.
- Really?

339
00:14:16,919 --> 00:14:19,120
- It seems split down the middle.
- I see.

340
00:14:19,421 --> 00:14:21,622
- So I'm still torn.
- Completely split.

341
00:14:22,358 --> 00:14:23,925
This is so hard. What should I do?

342
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:26,228
- There isn't much time.
- This is hard.

343
00:14:27,163 --> 00:14:28,797
There are ten minutes...

344
00:14:28,798 --> 00:14:31,066
- left to vote.
- Has anyone not voted?

345
00:14:32,368 --> 00:14:33,435
Those two haven't.

346
00:14:35,337 --> 00:14:36,704
We're voting separately, right?

347
00:14:38,107 --> 00:14:39,807
Elections aren't usually this hard.

348
00:14:39,808 --> 00:14:41,343
- Have you voted?
- Not yet.

349
00:14:41,344 --> 00:14:42,877
Go ahead if you're ready.

350
00:14:42,878 --> 00:14:45,046
- We should go last.
- We'll be last.

351
00:14:45,047 --> 00:14:47,449
- Okay.
- We'll vote for ourselves anyway.

352
00:14:52,555 --> 00:14:55,122
We're split exactly seven to six now.

353
00:14:55,123 --> 00:14:56,290
- Right.
- We're divided.

354
00:14:56,291 --> 00:14:58,559
The important thing is every single vote.

355
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:01,095
In a presidential election,
millions of people vote.

356
00:15:01,263 --> 00:15:02,997
But here, each vote has a direct impact.

357
00:15:02,998 --> 00:15:03,698
- Sure.
- Right.

358
00:15:03,699 --> 00:15:05,800
- That makes it even harder.
- Right.

359
00:15:05,935 --> 00:15:07,436
It isn't one vote out of 50 million.

360
00:15:07,437 --> 00:15:10,205
- Exactly.
- Each vote is incredibly powerful.

361
00:15:10,706 --> 00:15:12,373
This vote carries enormous weight.

362
00:15:12,374 --> 00:15:14,575
And for the next...

363
00:15:14,576 --> 00:15:16,144
three days we spend here,

364
00:15:16,145 --> 00:15:19,814
this will largely determine our course.

365
00:15:20,416 --> 00:15:22,050
So I can't decide rashly.

366
00:15:22,685 --> 00:15:23,518
This is so hard.

367
00:15:24,053 --> 00:15:26,321
Why does this have to be so hard?

368
00:15:26,924 --> 00:15:28,857
Why are they taking so long to vote?

369
00:15:29,024 --> 00:15:30,691
Right? They're really torn.

370
00:15:32,461 --> 00:15:34,829
- They're still talking over there.
- What are they doing?

371
00:15:35,397 --> 00:15:36,297
But...

372
00:15:36,599 --> 00:15:38,700
Genie is really calculating.

373
00:15:39,368 --> 00:15:40,268
Why?

374
00:15:40,569 --> 00:15:42,870
She isn't voting based on her beliefs.

375
00:15:42,871 --> 00:15:44,839
She doesn't want to vote
for the losing side.

376
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:46,207
- The losing side?
- Right.

377
00:15:46,375 --> 00:15:48,409
She's afraid of being disadvantaged.

378
00:15:48,711 --> 00:15:49,978
- That's...
- She's smart.

379
00:15:49,979 --> 00:15:51,079
That's smart.

380
00:15:51,513 --> 00:15:53,747
She went around asking everyone.

381
00:15:53,748 --> 00:15:55,216
Genie's still talking.

382
00:15:57,052 --> 00:15:59,320
Ted is impressive too.

383
00:15:59,722 --> 00:16:01,556
He's trying to vote last.

384
00:16:02,124 --> 00:16:03,357
To make his vote seem like the decider.

385
00:16:03,525 --> 00:16:04,525
He's quite something.

386
00:16:06,462 --> 00:16:07,762
Today really could...

387
00:16:07,763 --> 00:16:09,697
turn into another bloodbath.

388
00:16:10,666 --> 00:16:12,066
Everyone is...

389
00:16:12,067 --> 00:16:13,368
too unconcerned about money.

390
00:16:13,636 --> 00:16:15,737
They can do this because they're secure.

391
00:16:15,738 --> 00:16:19,140
But if the prize were 100,000 dollars,

392
00:16:19,275 --> 00:16:21,710
- wouldn't they be more motivated?
- Think about it.

393
00:16:22,244 --> 00:16:23,711
The more people...

394
00:16:25,047 --> 00:16:26,514
who die,

395
00:16:27,483 --> 00:16:29,417
the more prize money we can take.

396
00:16:30,853 --> 00:16:32,287
Honestly,

397
00:16:32,288 --> 00:16:34,556
I don't care much for idealism.

398
00:16:34,923 --> 00:16:36,156
How much do we get?

399
00:16:36,959 --> 00:16:38,359
It depends on us surviving...

400
00:16:38,694 --> 00:16:40,494
and how many people die.

401
00:16:42,331 --> 00:16:43,231
Gosh.

402
00:16:43,699 --> 00:16:45,266
- Voting closes...
- No.

403
00:16:45,267 --> 00:16:48,069
- in five minutes.
- How is time going so fast?

404
00:16:50,306 --> 00:16:51,340
I'm going.

405
00:16:51,341 --> 00:16:52,440
- Decided, Ae Shin?
- Wait.

406
00:16:52,441 --> 00:16:53,508
- Decided?
- On whom?

407
00:16:53,509 --> 00:16:54,576
- I'm going.
- I'm curious.

408
00:16:54,677 --> 00:16:56,011
Hurry up and go.

409
00:16:56,412 --> 00:16:58,480
I'll go out. I'll decide once I do.

410
00:16:58,481 --> 00:16:59,914
Just step outside.

411
00:16:59,915 --> 00:17:00,782
Let's go.

412
00:17:22,838 --> 00:17:23,738
I've decided.

413
00:17:27,309 --> 00:17:28,209
I don't know.

414
00:17:32,014 --> 00:17:34,249
- It isn't easy.
- I truly don't know.

415
00:17:34,250 --> 00:17:35,416
My head's going to explode.

416
00:17:35,417 --> 00:17:36,284
It's okay.

417
00:17:36,719 --> 00:17:38,019
My head's going to explode.

418
00:17:40,756 --> 00:17:42,290
(Polar Bear)

419
00:17:44,227 --> 00:17:45,693
Good job, me.

420
00:17:49,331 --> 00:17:50,298
Goodbye.

421
00:17:54,570 --> 00:17:55,803
(Superman)

422
00:17:58,474 --> 00:18:00,174
Voting is now complete.

423
00:18:00,175 --> 00:18:03,344
(All residents finish voting.)

424
00:18:03,979 --> 00:18:07,081
- Even I'm nervous.
- This is a Community Center announcement.

425
00:18:07,082 --> 00:18:08,015
Announcing it now?

426
00:18:08,016 --> 00:18:09,216
(Lifetime Leader announcement)

427
00:18:13,856 --> 00:18:14,956
Why am I so nervous?

428
00:18:16,325 --> 00:18:18,559
Here are the voting results.

429
00:18:22,798 --> 00:18:24,499
The voting results.

430
00:18:26,468 --> 00:18:28,936
With 11 votes to...

431
00:18:28,937 --> 00:18:31,205
(11 votes to...)

432
00:18:31,206 --> 00:18:33,174
two votes,

433
00:18:33,175 --> 00:18:35,576
(11 votes to 2 votes)

434
00:18:36,245 --> 00:18:44,752
With 11 votes to two,

435
00:18:47,723 --> 00:18:50,458
Polar Bear has been elected...

436
00:18:50,459 --> 00:18:52,694
as Lifetime Leader of the Community House.

437
00:18:52,928 --> 00:18:56,397
Polar Bear has been elected...

438
00:18:56,398 --> 00:18:58,666
as Lifetime Leader of the Community House.

439
00:18:59,067 --> 00:19:02,903
(An overwhelming margin of victory)

440
00:19:03,439 --> 00:19:04,839
Amazing.

441
00:19:06,842 --> 00:19:08,376
- Oh, my.
- No way.

442
00:19:08,477 --> 00:19:09,944
- What a margin.
- Congratulations.

443
00:19:11,013 --> 00:19:14,348
As Lifetime Leader, Polar Bear can't be...

444
00:19:14,450 --> 00:19:17,952
nominated for eviction during her stay.

445
00:19:31,166 --> 00:19:33,901
First, congratulations.

446
00:19:34,803 --> 00:19:35,836
Good work.

447
00:19:36,305 --> 00:19:37,005
Well done.

448
00:19:37,306 --> 00:19:38,593
- Good work.
- Well done.

449
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,575
- Superman too.
- Thank you.

450
00:19:41,743 --> 00:19:44,712
The margin was much wider than I expected.

451
00:19:46,081 --> 00:19:47,415
(Polar Bear versus Superman)

452
00:19:47,416 --> 00:19:48,682
(30 minutes earlier)

453
00:19:48,683 --> 00:19:50,317
The leader I chose is...

454
00:19:51,253 --> 00:19:52,086
Polar Bear.

455
00:19:52,087 --> 00:19:53,020
(Polar Bear is chosen.)

456
00:19:53,322 --> 00:19:54,622
Polar Bear.

457
00:19:54,623 --> 00:19:58,293
(Most residents vote for Polar Bear.)

458
00:20:02,831 --> 00:20:06,033
(Even the undecided Genie and Go Ae Shin
vote for Polar Bear.)

459
00:20:10,405 --> 00:20:11,839
(Superman)

460
00:20:14,676 --> 00:20:15,476
Superman.

461
00:20:17,779 --> 00:20:20,214
(Polar Bear: 11 votes, Superman: 2 votes)

462
00:20:24,286 --> 00:20:27,755
(The residents struggle to speak.)

463
00:20:30,893 --> 00:20:31,726
This is...

464
00:20:39,234 --> 00:20:42,836
The result was completely unexpected.

465
00:20:42,971 --> 00:20:45,506
Until this morning,

466
00:20:45,941 --> 00:20:48,943
I strongly supported Superman.

467
00:20:49,044 --> 00:20:51,679
I kept saying "we" and urged us
to keep fighting.

468
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:54,615
It was almost like we'd formed a campaign.

469
00:20:54,616 --> 00:20:59,353
But at the last moment,
I voted for Polar Bear.

470
00:21:00,056 --> 00:21:03,791
It's very fickle and embarrassing of me.

471
00:21:03,792 --> 00:21:05,526
But we don't know what game is next.

472
00:21:05,527 --> 00:21:08,163
I knew many people had chosen Polar Bear.

473
00:21:08,164 --> 00:21:10,331
- So most favor Polar Bear now?
- Most do.

474
00:21:10,899 --> 00:21:16,237
(Go Ae Shin gauges public opinion
with Genie before voting.)

475
00:21:17,773 --> 00:21:19,373
- Polar Bear.
- Really?

476
00:21:19,641 --> 00:21:21,275
They're leaning heavily one way.

477
00:21:21,343 --> 00:21:22,343
Really?

478
00:21:22,344 --> 00:21:25,680
It played on my fear
of ending up in the minority.

479
00:21:25,681 --> 00:21:27,048
That's what I think happened.

480
00:21:28,050 --> 00:21:29,017
It was shocking.

481
00:21:29,018 --> 00:21:32,653
I expected many people
to support Superman.

482
00:21:32,654 --> 00:21:34,555
Because Superman promised...

483
00:21:34,556 --> 00:21:36,758
to let each person keep...

484
00:21:36,759 --> 00:21:37,925
what they earned.

485
00:21:37,926 --> 00:21:39,894
He promised to maximize their gains.

486
00:21:39,895 --> 00:21:41,629
I expected that to sway many people.

487
00:21:41,630 --> 00:21:43,564
But Polar Bear won 11 to 2.

488
00:21:44,333 --> 00:21:45,833
Until right before the speeches,

489
00:21:45,834 --> 00:21:48,403
I thought I might vote for Superman.

490
00:21:48,737 --> 00:21:50,672
He strongly declared
that he would impose...

491
00:21:50,673 --> 00:21:52,240
punitive taxes on anyone...

492
00:21:52,241 --> 00:21:55,009
who behaved like a traitor.

493
00:21:55,010 --> 00:21:57,078
This may sound contradictory.

494
00:21:57,478 --> 00:21:59,546
But while I want communal well-being,

495
00:21:59,547 --> 00:22:03,819
I want our direction to emerge...

496
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:05,619
from everyone's voluntary agreement.

497
00:22:05,754 --> 00:22:08,522
I wondered if coercion was right.

498
00:22:08,824 --> 00:22:12,226
When I heard that pledge from Superman,

499
00:22:12,227 --> 00:22:13,628
(Right, feminism,
upper-middle, open-minded)

500
00:22:13,629 --> 00:22:18,065
I thought I might have voted for him
without that part.

501
00:22:19,468 --> 00:22:20,935
Even after yesterday's debate,

502
00:22:20,936 --> 00:22:23,905
I was leaning toward Superman.

503
00:22:24,039 --> 00:22:26,407
But Polar Bear seemed most likely...

504
00:22:26,408 --> 00:22:29,310
to put our survival first
and minimize the risk.

505
00:22:30,045 --> 00:22:32,546
So I ended up favoring Polar Bear.

506
00:22:32,881 --> 00:22:34,949
Since she could ensure my survival too,

507
00:22:34,950 --> 00:22:37,751
I cast my vote for Polar Bear.

508
00:22:37,752 --> 00:22:40,754
I chose what could keep me alive now.

509
00:22:40,755 --> 00:22:43,123
She seemed likely to save me
even if I were eliminated.

510
00:22:43,325 --> 00:22:46,060
I think Polar Bear read the room well.

511
00:22:46,428 --> 00:22:49,430
What matters most to the people here?

512
00:22:49,431 --> 00:22:50,297
Survival.

513
00:22:51,066 --> 00:22:52,566
I voted for Polar Bear.

514
00:22:52,567 --> 00:22:56,037
She's a very promising young woman.

515
00:22:56,038 --> 00:22:58,806
I may sound old-fashioned,
but I want to teach her a lesson.

516
00:22:59,007 --> 00:23:00,174
That you shouldn't trust people.

517
00:23:00,175 --> 00:23:03,210
To monsters like Benjamin,

518
00:23:03,211 --> 00:23:05,246
this is nothing. It's child's play.

519
00:23:05,247 --> 00:23:06,513
It's almost cute.

520
00:23:06,715 --> 00:23:07,882
Maybe she'll learn this time.

521
00:23:08,050 --> 00:23:09,150
That's how the world works.

522
00:23:10,285 --> 00:23:11,852
As for Polar Bear,

523
00:23:11,853 --> 00:23:14,888
she's far too idealistic.

524
00:23:14,889 --> 00:23:17,358
Superman was a better fit for me.

525
00:23:17,759 --> 00:23:19,126
I think I was his only voter.

526
00:23:22,531 --> 00:23:25,967
(Awkwardness fills the Community.)

527
00:23:35,077 --> 00:23:36,944
- Let's take a ten-minute break.
- Okay.

528
00:23:36,945 --> 00:23:37,912
Let's take ten minutes.

529
00:23:38,146 --> 00:23:39,279
Let's get some air together.

530
00:23:46,755 --> 00:23:48,456
I'm worried this will get awkward.

531
00:23:49,758 --> 00:23:50,591
Hang in there.

532
00:23:53,295 --> 00:23:54,695
Just act like you always do.

533
00:23:54,896 --> 00:23:57,097
- Of course.
- You have many good ideas.

534
00:23:57,299 --> 00:23:59,166
I'm going to stay quiet for a day or two.

535
00:23:59,534 --> 00:24:00,400
Because...

536
00:24:00,869 --> 00:24:03,637
what I said clearly didn't appeal...

537
00:24:03,638 --> 00:24:05,840
to the members of the Community.

538
00:24:05,941 --> 00:24:09,110
I'll give the leader more room to speak.

539
00:24:09,945 --> 00:24:12,380
I think I'd better stay quiet for a while.

540
00:24:12,647 --> 00:24:13,547
I think that's best.

541
00:24:25,227 --> 00:24:27,628
I'll go get a glass of water.

542
00:24:29,498 --> 00:24:30,531
What do I do?

543
00:24:30,799 --> 00:24:33,033
But what if this was all planned?

544
00:24:33,602 --> 00:24:35,903
By that side? The spy's side?

545
00:24:35,904 --> 00:24:37,171
You don't think so?

546
00:24:37,873 --> 00:24:39,340
What do we do?

547
00:24:39,341 --> 00:24:41,075
The margin is so huge.

548
00:24:41,076 --> 00:24:42,243
I had no idea it'd end up like this.

549
00:24:42,477 --> 00:24:44,715
This is serious. And Superman earlier...

550
00:24:44,716 --> 00:24:46,448
- He couldn't hide it.
- was furious.

551
00:24:46,449 --> 00:24:48,315
His pride is at stake too.

552
00:24:48,316 --> 00:24:49,817
He worried about that.

553
00:24:49,818 --> 00:24:52,386
That he'd look bad if he lost the vote.

554
00:24:52,387 --> 00:24:54,021
From what people said earlier,

555
00:24:54,456 --> 00:24:56,690
they didn't vote for Superman,

556
00:24:56,691 --> 00:24:57,758
because he's too forceful.

557
00:24:57,759 --> 00:24:59,227
His personality is too strong.

558
00:24:59,228 --> 00:25:01,062
They think he'll insist on his way.

559
00:25:01,063 --> 00:25:03,998
They want this country run their way too.

560
00:25:03,999 --> 00:25:05,232
But he's too forceful.

561
00:25:05,233 --> 00:25:07,034
They think he won't give them room.

562
00:25:07,536 --> 00:25:09,604
In my case, they want me...

563
00:25:09,605 --> 00:25:11,506
to be nice and easygoing.

564
00:25:11,507 --> 00:25:12,406
That's part of it.

565
00:25:12,574 --> 00:25:13,440
That's possible.

566
00:25:13,742 --> 00:25:15,643
That's why we need Superman too.

567
00:25:15,844 --> 00:25:17,311
I should rethink our strategy with him.

568
00:25:17,312 --> 00:25:19,445
But I feel bad even talking to him.

569
00:25:19,446 --> 00:25:20,648
I don't know what to do.

570
00:25:21,149 --> 00:25:23,984
People are more afraid than they look.

571
00:25:23,985 --> 00:25:26,920
As soon as I saw the number 11,

572
00:25:27,889 --> 00:25:30,657
I realized they're more afraid
than I thought.

573
00:25:30,692 --> 00:25:33,761
Above all, they want to survive...

574
00:25:34,062 --> 00:25:38,599
until the end and take home prize money.

575
00:25:38,600 --> 00:25:40,134
That means very few of them believe...

576
00:25:40,135 --> 00:25:42,836
they can come in first.

577
00:25:42,837 --> 00:25:44,204
Right now, they all see...

578
00:25:44,872 --> 00:25:46,774
themselves as potential evictees.

579
00:25:46,775 --> 00:25:47,708
They want to live.

580
00:25:53,448 --> 00:25:55,015
(Superman)

581
00:26:06,127 --> 00:26:09,296
I thought about it a lot afterward.

582
00:26:09,497 --> 00:26:12,299
To me, it wasn't
simply losing an election.

583
00:26:12,300 --> 00:26:15,102
It cut very deep.

584
00:26:15,103 --> 00:26:17,437
Even when I lost
the National Assembly race,

585
00:26:17,873 --> 00:26:20,775
I didn't feel anything cut this deep.

586
00:26:20,776 --> 00:26:23,544
Maybe it was because of the result,

587
00:26:24,379 --> 00:26:26,947
but it cut very deeply.

588
00:26:26,948 --> 00:26:28,115
That's how I felt.

589
00:26:28,216 --> 00:26:30,751
I thought more people might agree with me.

590
00:26:30,752 --> 00:26:33,120
That's what I believed.

591
00:26:33,121 --> 00:26:35,022
But it wasn't even close.

592
00:26:35,323 --> 00:26:37,124
"We can't agree with you..."

593
00:26:37,559 --> 00:26:39,527
was what the result practically meant.

594
00:26:39,594 --> 00:26:42,196
Superman's words utterly failed...

595
00:26:42,631 --> 00:26:44,599
to win their hearts.

596
00:26:44,865 --> 00:26:47,000
I failed to pinpoint...

597
00:26:47,001 --> 00:26:50,170
what they wanted or feared.

598
00:26:50,672 --> 00:26:52,640
It gave me a lot to reflect on.

599
00:26:53,341 --> 00:26:55,475
The people I meet in person...

600
00:26:55,476 --> 00:26:57,377
who like and greet me...

601
00:26:57,545 --> 00:27:00,413
may vote differently in the voting booth.

602
00:27:01,149 --> 00:27:03,751
There is a gap between what lies...

603
00:27:03,752 --> 00:27:05,119
on the surface and underneath.

604
00:27:05,954 --> 00:27:08,389
I'd been arrogant enough to think
I understood it well.

605
00:27:08,790 --> 00:27:11,859
I seriously considered that today.

606
00:27:11,860 --> 00:27:14,328
I don't like telling people
what they want to hear.

607
00:27:14,562 --> 00:27:17,664
I prefer telling them harsh truths.

608
00:27:18,033 --> 00:27:18,933
But...

609
00:27:19,567 --> 00:27:21,134
do people like that?

610
00:27:21,670 --> 00:27:24,104
Is that the virtue of a good politician?

611
00:27:24,105 --> 00:27:25,706
I thought a lot about that.

612
00:27:26,041 --> 00:27:28,175
Nevertheless, I'll accept it gracefully...

613
00:27:28,276 --> 00:27:30,577
and help Polar Bear become...

614
00:27:30,578 --> 00:27:32,746
a good leader.

615
00:27:35,985 --> 00:27:37,984
The fact that so many people voted...

616
00:27:37,985 --> 00:27:39,454
for me means...

617
00:27:39,455 --> 00:27:41,955
they felt threatened by elimination.

618
00:27:42,157 --> 00:27:44,325
I thought their desire...

619
00:27:44,326 --> 00:27:47,394
to survive here had coalesced around me.

620
00:27:47,629 --> 00:27:49,797
Apart from our pledges,

621
00:27:50,198 --> 00:27:52,065
when comparing me with Superman...

622
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:54,401
and our personal traits,

623
00:27:54,402 --> 00:27:58,438
I may have seemed a little more lenient.

624
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:02,576
Superman may be smarter and wiser than me.

625
00:28:02,944 --> 00:28:05,345
His principles are firm and clear.

626
00:28:05,513 --> 00:28:07,414
But the residents may have felt...

627
00:28:08,016 --> 00:28:10,117
that he couldn't embrace those...

628
00:28:10,118 --> 00:28:12,253
who think differently from him.

629
00:28:12,254 --> 00:28:13,321
I'd considered that.

630
00:28:13,521 --> 00:28:15,722
A leader's pledges matter.

631
00:28:15,723 --> 00:28:17,891
But ultimately, their character...

632
00:28:18,059 --> 00:28:22,329
and attitude may have mattered more
to the voters.

633
00:28:22,330 --> 00:28:24,931
That's what the result made me think.

634
00:28:24,932 --> 00:28:26,700
Still, the margin was so wide...

635
00:28:27,336 --> 00:28:28,302
that I was shocked.

636
00:28:32,607 --> 00:28:35,142
Leader, please visit
the Community Center...

637
00:28:35,143 --> 00:28:37,444
to collect the Leader's Box.

638
00:28:43,651 --> 00:28:47,687
(Polar Bear, Lifetime Leader: left,
feminism, working-class, open-minded)

639
00:28:47,688 --> 00:28:50,156
Congratulations on becoming the leader.

640
00:28:56,031 --> 00:28:58,099
You may amend one rule...

641
00:28:58,334 --> 00:29:00,534
of the Community House.

642
00:29:03,071 --> 00:29:04,338
I have to do it in 30 minutes?

643
00:29:04,339 --> 00:29:05,939
(Rule amendment and tax meeting)

644
00:29:05,940 --> 00:29:07,774
We only have 30 minutes.

645
00:29:07,775 --> 00:29:10,010
But we also have to set today's tax.

646
00:29:10,678 --> 00:29:11,945
Right, we have to decide.

647
00:29:11,946 --> 00:29:13,847
We all have some personal funds.

648
00:29:13,848 --> 00:29:14,981
We tax daily, right?

649
00:29:14,982 --> 00:29:16,416
Taxes are deducted daily.

650
00:29:16,417 --> 00:29:17,517
We have to do it again.

651
00:29:18,153 --> 00:29:20,221
This is crazy. We earned nothing today.

652
00:29:20,222 --> 00:29:21,222
- Exactly.
- Right.

653
00:29:22,257 --> 00:29:24,758
Should we discuss the tax rate first?

654
00:29:24,759 --> 00:29:28,262
Today's rate should be simple.

655
00:29:30,432 --> 00:29:32,900
Should we just have ramyeon for dinner?

656
00:29:32,901 --> 00:29:34,635
- Ramyeon sounds good.
- I like that.

657
00:29:34,636 --> 00:29:36,070
Let's add rice to the broth.

658
00:29:36,071 --> 00:29:37,805
This is the first time you guys have
accepted my idea.

659
00:29:38,073 --> 00:29:39,340
For the first time.

660
00:29:40,241 --> 00:29:42,810
Because you finally said something right.

661
00:29:42,877 --> 00:29:45,846
But one of Superman's pledges was...

662
00:29:46,114 --> 00:29:48,082
- to collect less and eat less.
- Right.

663
00:29:48,083 --> 00:29:51,018
- I really agreed with that.
- Me too.

664
00:29:51,419 --> 00:29:54,621
We couldn't earn any money today.

665
00:29:54,889 --> 00:29:57,257
So to protect your money,

666
00:29:57,258 --> 00:29:59,826
- I propose a ten percent tax.
- Okay.

667
00:29:59,827 --> 00:30:01,261
- Does everyone agree?
- Sounds good.

668
00:30:01,262 --> 00:30:02,529
- Yes.
- Sounds good.

669
00:30:02,530 --> 00:30:03,430
All right.

670
00:30:05,166 --> 00:30:07,167
I didn't want to speak today.

671
00:30:07,168 --> 00:30:08,535
As the person who lost,

672
00:30:08,536 --> 00:30:10,637
I thought I should give the leader space.

673
00:30:10,638 --> 00:30:13,039
My forced smile might bother people.

674
00:30:13,308 --> 00:30:15,776
But my silence might bother them too.

675
00:30:15,977 --> 00:30:18,879
So I decided to sit and quietly observe.

676
00:30:24,819 --> 00:30:26,586
I keep bringing everyone down.

677
00:30:26,821 --> 00:30:28,288
- We're just thinking.
- Not at all.

678
00:30:28,289 --> 00:30:29,589
We can't think of any ideas.

679
00:30:29,590 --> 00:30:30,857
I'm a little sleepy too.

680
00:30:31,059 --> 00:30:32,226
- I'll go.
- Take it easy.

681
00:30:32,227 --> 00:30:33,360
Talk freely. It's okay.

682
00:30:37,499 --> 00:30:38,532
This is sad.

683
00:30:46,908 --> 00:30:47,908
(Superman)

684
00:30:47,909 --> 00:30:48,776
Gosh.

685
00:30:53,681 --> 00:30:55,248
All that's left is the rule.

686
00:30:55,249 --> 00:30:56,549
(Rule amendment meeting)

687
00:30:56,550 --> 00:30:59,152
When I considered the rules,

688
00:30:59,153 --> 00:31:00,587
I wondered...

689
00:31:00,689 --> 00:31:03,156
what you might be dissatisfied with.

690
00:31:03,157 --> 00:31:04,291
Ultimately, I thought...

691
00:31:04,292 --> 00:31:06,259
it was the communal fund rule.

692
00:31:06,827 --> 00:31:08,595
And your original pledge was...

693
00:31:09,430 --> 00:31:13,323
(Polar Bear pledges to distribute
the leader's daily personal fund...)

694
00:31:13,324 --> 00:31:17,103
(to the person with the least money.)

695
00:31:17,639 --> 00:31:19,139
But then,

696
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:21,808
how will we know everyone's balance?

697
00:31:21,809 --> 00:31:24,678
People are far too likely to lie.

698
00:31:25,380 --> 00:31:26,580
I'll report mine honestly.

699
00:31:26,681 --> 00:31:27,681
I'll underreport mine.

700
00:31:27,682 --> 00:31:29,049
I'll report mine honestly.

701
00:31:29,050 --> 00:31:31,118
I'll say I have zero dollars.

702
00:31:31,386 --> 00:31:32,353
How devious.

703
00:31:32,820 --> 00:31:34,420
- Scold her.
- How devious.

704
00:31:35,790 --> 00:31:37,758
Right. Someone won't reveal it all.

705
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:42,229
Here is the communal fund rule.

706
00:31:42,230 --> 00:31:44,064
"The communal fund is for everyone."

707
00:31:44,265 --> 00:31:46,833
"Any money remaining after your stay..."

708
00:31:46,834 --> 00:31:48,635
"will be used for everyone."

709
00:31:48,636 --> 00:31:50,837
That line stood out to me today.

710
00:31:51,105 --> 00:31:52,272
We currently think...

711
00:31:52,273 --> 00:31:54,074
the communal fund isn't ours...

712
00:31:54,075 --> 00:31:56,510
because it isn't in our personal accounts.

713
00:31:56,511 --> 00:31:57,877
- Collect more...
- I love this.

714
00:31:57,878 --> 00:31:59,413
and if we have plenty left later,

715
00:31:59,414 --> 00:32:00,914
it will be used for everyone.

716
00:32:00,915 --> 00:32:02,315
Since it's everyone's money,

717
00:32:02,316 --> 00:32:03,850
I think it will be divided among us.

718
00:32:03,851 --> 00:32:04,818
We could amend it.

719
00:32:04,819 --> 00:32:06,586
Should we say it will be split evenly?

720
00:32:07,455 --> 00:32:09,756
Then we'd feel less burdened...

721
00:32:09,757 --> 00:32:10,891
by paying into it.

722
00:32:10,892 --> 00:32:12,125
Sounds good.

723
00:32:13,094 --> 00:32:14,428
With a healthy communal fund,

724
00:32:14,429 --> 00:32:16,263
- we have more options.
- Right.

725
00:32:16,531 --> 00:32:18,298
The current wording is ambiguous.

726
00:32:18,299 --> 00:32:19,633
Let's make it clear.

727
00:32:19,835 --> 00:32:22,302
Any communal funds left after your stay...

728
00:32:22,303 --> 00:32:24,972
- will be divided among us.
- Divided among everyone.

729
00:32:26,040 --> 00:32:27,941
But here's what I'm thinking.

730
00:32:27,942 --> 00:32:30,611
The amount accumulating there isn't huge.

731
00:32:30,612 --> 00:32:32,313
Even if it's 6,000 dollars,

732
00:32:32,314 --> 00:32:34,414
each person gets under 500 dollars.

733
00:32:34,749 --> 00:32:35,749
Would an even split...

734
00:32:35,750 --> 00:32:37,551
really make a difference?

735
00:32:37,552 --> 00:32:39,920
We should keep that in mind too.

736
00:32:40,255 --> 00:32:43,791
First, abolish the 1,000 dollars
the leader receives from the fund.

737
00:32:44,158 --> 00:32:46,126
But if that first option fails,

738
00:32:46,127 --> 00:32:48,161
then 1,000 dollars will be
paid out each day.

739
00:32:48,363 --> 00:32:50,497
- Right.
- Then little will remain.

740
00:32:50,698 --> 00:32:51,531
Even if divided.

741
00:32:52,634 --> 00:32:54,935
What if they make us buy
everything on the menu?

742
00:32:55,103 --> 00:32:56,437
For everyone.

743
00:32:57,505 --> 00:32:59,039
They might make us buy it all.

744
00:33:00,675 --> 00:33:02,843
In the final game, the spy can...

745
00:33:03,312 --> 00:33:05,979
only take the final prize money...

746
00:33:05,980 --> 00:33:07,381
the residents have accumulated.

747
00:33:09,117 --> 00:33:13,286
Therefore, the less money transferred
to the communal fund,

748
00:33:13,514 --> 00:33:16,123
the more prize money the spy can take.

749
00:33:17,124 --> 00:33:18,125
I just didn't like it.

750
00:33:18,126 --> 00:33:19,893
I want to get in their way.

751
00:33:19,894 --> 00:33:21,694
Even without my intervention,

752
00:33:21,695 --> 00:33:23,630
they already treat saving funds as a sin.

753
00:33:23,931 --> 00:33:25,632
We have to choose between two options.

754
00:33:25,633 --> 00:33:27,133
If we abolish that payment,

755
00:33:27,134 --> 00:33:28,902
the 4,000 dollars meant for the leader...

756
00:33:28,903 --> 00:33:30,870
will remain in the fund.

757
00:33:30,871 --> 00:33:33,273
That will ease the burden...

758
00:33:33,274 --> 00:33:34,407
of paying into it.

759
00:33:34,408 --> 00:33:35,475
If we divide the fund,

760
00:33:35,476 --> 00:33:36,943
the 1,000 dollars still gets paid out.

761
00:33:36,944 --> 00:33:38,512
So 4,000 dollars will go there.

762
00:33:38,513 --> 00:33:39,779
Then the remaining money stays...

763
00:33:39,780 --> 00:33:41,313
in the fund.

764
00:33:41,314 --> 00:33:42,451
- Then.
- The funds left.

765
00:33:42,452 --> 00:33:43,850
If there's 1,000 dollars left...

766
00:33:43,851 --> 00:33:46,819
on the last day,
the 13 of us will split it.

767
00:33:46,954 --> 00:33:47,854
That's the idea.

768
00:33:48,323 --> 00:33:49,723
So abolish it or divide it?

769
00:33:50,858 --> 00:33:51,825
End the leader's pay?

770
00:33:51,826 --> 00:33:53,560
I think abolishing it is better.

771
00:33:53,561 --> 00:33:55,395
Erase that rule? All right.

772
00:33:55,563 --> 00:33:56,963
My vote is to divide it.

773
00:33:57,165 --> 00:33:58,633
Even if my view doesn't prevail,

774
00:33:58,634 --> 00:33:59,967
I'll still make my opinion known.

775
00:34:01,969 --> 00:34:03,236
Then one last vote.

776
00:34:03,237 --> 00:34:06,139
Who favors dividing it
into our personal funds?

777
00:34:06,908 --> 00:34:08,008
Raise your hand freely.

778
00:34:08,376 --> 00:34:09,142
(Sugar, Hippo)

779
00:34:09,411 --> 00:34:11,244
Who favors ending the payment?

780
00:34:11,846 --> 00:34:13,346
(No payout: all but Sugar and Hippo)

781
00:34:13,347 --> 00:34:16,016
All right. I'll go submit that.

782
00:34:16,385 --> 00:34:19,186
Each person would receive so little.

783
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:21,588
(The Community Center)

784
00:34:21,589 --> 00:34:24,157
(One Community House rule may be
added, amended, or deleted.)

785
00:34:24,292 --> 00:34:26,693
(The leader's 1,000-dollar payment is
abolished.)

786
00:34:27,061 --> 00:34:30,363
I think we'll keep having to choose...

787
00:34:30,364 --> 00:34:32,899
between the communal fund
and our personal gain.

788
00:34:32,900 --> 00:34:35,468
We see it differently from the others,
but majority rules.

789
00:34:36,771 --> 00:34:37,938
Thanks for agreeing with me.

790
00:34:40,174 --> 00:34:41,141
Don't mention it.

791
00:34:42,510 --> 00:34:44,511
I still wanted to voice my opinion.

792
00:34:44,746 --> 00:34:47,348
- Good job.
- Even if it didn't win them over.

793
00:34:47,915 --> 00:34:48,748
Remember that.

794
00:34:53,621 --> 00:34:55,889
Hippo is so assertive now.

795
00:34:57,091 --> 00:34:58,024
Hippo.

796
00:34:58,292 --> 00:34:59,459
She's changed a lot.

797
00:35:00,561 --> 00:35:01,694
Wasn't she always like that?

798
00:35:02,230 --> 00:35:03,096
She was quiet.

799
00:35:03,965 --> 00:35:06,266
From Day One until now,

800
00:35:06,267 --> 00:35:08,502
Hippo has changed the most.

801
00:35:08,736 --> 00:35:10,437
She's extremely excited now.

802
00:35:11,239 --> 00:35:12,639
But that's poisonous.

803
00:35:13,107 --> 00:35:16,510
She suddenly changed,
sat at the center of the table,

804
00:35:16,511 --> 00:35:18,512
and talked like the main character.

805
00:35:18,513 --> 00:35:20,080
She's trying to lead.

806
00:35:20,481 --> 00:35:22,749
No matter how much you care
for people like that,

807
00:35:23,117 --> 00:35:25,685
they're very likely to betray you.

808
00:35:26,154 --> 00:35:28,655
(Day Two Prize Distribution Drawing)

809
00:35:28,756 --> 00:35:29,656
Nothing now, right?

810
00:35:30,358 --> 00:35:32,025
Me? Yeah. I got nothing.

811
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:33,594
Give my share to Hippo.

812
00:35:33,861 --> 00:35:36,196
(Dark Knight gives his prize to Hippo.)

813
00:35:36,431 --> 00:35:37,197
The price for a heart.

814
00:35:38,099 --> 00:35:38,832
Will do.

815
00:35:38,833 --> 00:35:43,370
(Dark Knight asks for a heart in exchange
for 1,000 dollars.)

816
00:35:44,972 --> 00:35:46,406
(Michael)

817
00:35:46,407 --> 00:35:48,041
(Sugar)

818
00:35:48,042 --> 00:35:49,709
(Genie)

819
00:35:50,111 --> 00:35:54,047
(Hippo does not give Dark Knight
a favorability vote.)

820
00:35:54,416 --> 00:35:55,850
Even after that, Hippo...

821
00:35:55,851 --> 00:35:57,450
never thanked me once.

822
00:35:57,552 --> 00:35:58,485
Funny, isn't it?

823
00:35:58,586 --> 00:36:01,788
People who are used to taking
are usually like that.

824
00:36:03,891 --> 00:36:07,627
Ten percent
of each resident's personal funds...

825
00:36:07,628 --> 00:36:09,495
have been collected for the communal fund.

826
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:14,200
We've got plenty of money.

827
00:36:14,302 --> 00:36:15,369
That's a lot.

828
00:36:16,405 --> 00:36:19,673
An existing Community House rule
has been repealed.

829
00:36:20,541 --> 00:36:22,108
The repealed rule stated...

830
00:36:22,543 --> 00:36:27,580
that the leader would receive
1,000 dollars from the communal fund.

831
00:36:28,148 --> 00:36:31,217
This change applies to the current fund.

832
00:36:31,218 --> 00:36:33,420
- Good work.
- You too.

833
00:36:35,089 --> 00:36:38,291
(Ten percent collected
for the communal fund)

834
00:36:38,292 --> 00:36:42,429
(Leader's personal fund stipend removed)

835
00:36:43,130 --> 00:36:45,698
I'd like to discuss
the Reporter's question.

836
00:36:45,699 --> 00:36:46,899
Let's have a seat.

837
00:36:48,669 --> 00:36:49,669
Did you get any rest?

838
00:36:50,005 --> 00:36:51,204
I got a little sleep.

839
00:36:51,339 --> 00:36:52,372
Good.

840
00:36:54,042 --> 00:36:56,042
We already have the question framed.

841
00:36:56,043 --> 00:36:59,512
- We talked about it this morning.
- Okay.

842
00:36:59,513 --> 00:37:00,413
So...

843
00:37:00,414 --> 00:37:01,881
(This morning)

844
00:37:01,882 --> 00:37:04,851
I think we need to settle...

845
00:37:05,052 --> 00:37:07,987
that first issue once and for all.

846
00:37:07,988 --> 00:37:09,322
The number of hearts.

847
00:37:09,724 --> 00:37:11,124
The tampered heart count.

848
00:37:11,659 --> 00:37:14,094
(Hippo brings up
Michael's single vote again.)

849
00:37:14,095 --> 00:37:16,396
We need a question that puts this to rest.

850
00:37:17,431 --> 00:37:19,933
Someone might have just misvoted.

851
00:37:19,934 --> 00:37:23,370
But all morning,
she kept pushing that same question.

852
00:37:23,371 --> 00:37:26,940
That was the moment I became certain
Hippo was suspicious.

853
00:37:26,941 --> 00:37:29,309
I don't think it's a big deal.

854
00:37:29,644 --> 00:37:31,945
Why does it keep coming up?

855
00:37:31,946 --> 00:37:33,614
I actually don't understand.

856
00:37:33,814 --> 00:37:36,015
We had even forgotten about it
until today.

857
00:37:36,016 --> 00:37:40,253
Is that really worth suspecting
someone over?

858
00:37:40,254 --> 00:37:42,188
It only made her look more suspicious.

859
00:37:42,657 --> 00:37:45,058
So we settled on this question.

860
00:37:45,059 --> 00:37:48,128
Michael said he received one vote
on Day One.

861
00:37:48,396 --> 00:37:51,465
Gray and Dark Knight both claim
they voted for Michael.

862
00:37:51,466 --> 00:37:54,968
Which of the three lied?

863
00:37:54,969 --> 00:37:55,902
That question...

864
00:38:00,841 --> 00:38:04,310
I mean, it will either narrow down
or blow open...

865
00:38:04,311 --> 00:38:07,246
our pool of spy suspects.

866
00:38:07,815 --> 00:38:08,782
Understood.

867
00:38:09,116 --> 00:38:11,084
Once it came down to two suspects,

868
00:38:11,319 --> 00:38:14,621
our path felt much clearer.

869
00:38:14,622 --> 00:38:16,824
There's a spy among us...

870
00:38:16,825 --> 00:38:20,060
trying to tear us apart.

871
00:38:20,461 --> 00:38:23,063
I figured if we kept a close eye out,

872
00:38:23,064 --> 00:38:25,198
we could catch them.

873
00:38:25,199 --> 00:38:27,068
I suddenly felt a rush of motivation.

874
00:38:27,069 --> 00:38:28,735
I wanted to catch the spy.

875
00:38:29,470 --> 00:38:30,637
Shall we go ask now?

876
00:38:30,638 --> 00:38:31,871
Sure. Go right ahead.

877
00:38:34,909 --> 00:38:37,445
I'm the Reporter. I'm here for my inquiry.

878
00:38:37,745 --> 00:38:40,080
The Reporter's inquiry begins.

879
00:38:40,348 --> 00:38:42,015
I never should have brought it up.

880
00:38:42,016 --> 00:38:43,817
I shouldn't have mentioned it back then.

881
00:38:43,818 --> 00:38:44,984
Right. I'm sorry.

882
00:38:44,985 --> 00:38:46,486
Who knew it would...

883
00:38:46,787 --> 00:38:48,154
drag on like this until today?

884
00:38:48,155 --> 00:38:49,322
Hippo says she's feeling anxious.

885
00:38:49,323 --> 00:38:50,723
Really anxious.

886
00:38:50,724 --> 00:38:52,492
Getting rid of that uncertainty...

887
00:38:52,493 --> 00:38:53,526
- isn't a bad idea.
- Exactly.

888
00:38:54,028 --> 00:38:55,261
It'll clear the air, too.

889
00:39:03,070 --> 00:39:05,004
May I announce the result?

890
00:39:05,206 --> 00:39:07,007
Michael stated that on Day One...

891
00:39:07,008 --> 00:39:10,243
he received a single favorability vote.

892
00:39:10,745 --> 00:39:12,212
"Which of the three..."

893
00:39:12,213 --> 00:39:15,315
"made a false statement?"

894
00:39:15,316 --> 00:39:16,650
That was the question.

895
00:39:16,985 --> 00:39:17,951
The answer is...

896
00:39:25,093 --> 00:39:28,295
Dark Knight was the one lying.

897
00:39:28,963 --> 00:39:30,330
It was Dark Knight.

898
00:39:30,765 --> 00:39:34,668
(Dark Knight was the one lying.)

899
00:39:35,370 --> 00:39:37,004
That really isn't how it went down.

900
00:39:37,371 --> 00:39:39,739
I get it. You have every reason
to doubt me.

901
00:39:43,778 --> 00:39:45,879
Go ahead and suspect me.
I brought this on myself.

902
00:39:46,514 --> 00:39:47,380
Right.

903
00:39:49,750 --> 00:39:52,219
I'm truly sorry.
I caused all this confusion.

904
00:39:52,220 --> 00:39:53,319
- It's fine.
- Yeah.

905
00:39:53,888 --> 00:39:55,922
(Day Two Interview)

906
00:39:56,023 --> 00:39:58,825
I don't remember
who I wrote down yesterday...

907
00:39:58,826 --> 00:40:00,960
simply because it didn't matter to me.

908
00:40:00,961 --> 00:40:02,663
Even today, I had no...

909
00:40:02,664 --> 00:40:05,164
real reason behind my pick.

910
00:40:05,165 --> 00:40:06,863
(Dark Knight's votes: Nangja, Sugar, Ted)

911
00:40:06,863 --> 00:40:08,134
(No Michael)

912
00:40:09,904 --> 00:40:11,338
You don't need to remember.

913
00:40:11,639 --> 00:40:13,773
(Gray's Day One favorability vote)

914
00:40:13,774 --> 00:40:15,976
(Michael)

915
00:40:16,610 --> 00:40:21,147
(A misunderstanding born
from a casual favor)

916
00:40:21,449 --> 00:40:25,185
Maybe my memory has been
off since day one.

917
00:40:25,186 --> 00:40:26,820
I honestly can't say.

918
00:40:26,921 --> 00:40:30,023
Still, it snowballed,
drew everyone's attention...

919
00:40:30,024 --> 00:40:31,558
and caused such a stir.

920
00:40:31,959 --> 00:40:34,294
And now it's come to this.

921
00:40:35,363 --> 00:40:36,829
That's my bad.

922
00:40:37,698 --> 00:40:41,000
Anything I say just sounds like an excuse.
I'm sorry.

923
00:40:42,303 --> 00:40:43,336
I apologize.

924
00:40:43,337 --> 00:40:44,604
I feel awful about this.

925
00:40:46,540 --> 00:40:49,308
Going off this info,

926
00:40:49,443 --> 00:40:52,445
Michael seems much less likely
to be the spy.

927
00:40:53,314 --> 00:40:54,147
I agree.

928
00:40:54,482 --> 00:40:55,482
Still, I...

929
00:40:57,184 --> 00:41:00,987
don't think this clears him completely.

930
00:41:00,988 --> 00:41:02,155
- Me neither.
- Same here.

931
00:41:02,790 --> 00:41:04,958
Just because I didn't lie about this...

932
00:41:04,959 --> 00:41:07,260
doesn't mean I can't be the spy.

933
00:41:07,261 --> 00:41:11,164
Even with all the Reporter's findings...

934
00:41:11,365 --> 00:41:13,399
and everything we can confirm,

935
00:41:13,400 --> 00:41:15,968
I don't think we can definitively prove
anyone is the spy.

936
00:41:15,969 --> 00:41:18,071
That would be nearly impossible.

937
00:41:18,072 --> 00:41:22,108
So this doesn't clear him.

938
00:41:22,109 --> 00:41:23,810
- I said it's less likely.
- Less likely, right.

939
00:41:23,811 --> 00:41:25,244
- That's all I said.
- Less likely.

940
00:41:25,346 --> 00:41:27,213
And I'm saying it doesn't make
him any less likely.

941
00:41:27,214 --> 00:41:28,815
Okay, fair enough.

942
00:41:37,992 --> 00:41:40,360
At the end of the day, this was all on me.

943
00:41:40,428 --> 00:41:42,595
I let things spiral out of control.

944
00:41:42,596 --> 00:41:44,363
I'm sorry about that.

945
00:41:44,364 --> 00:41:46,599
My sincere apologies.

946
00:41:48,836 --> 00:41:49,869
This is driving me crazy.

947
00:41:52,373 --> 00:41:54,042
So, what about dinner?

948
00:41:54,043 --> 00:41:55,976
- We should eat.
- Ramyeon.

949
00:41:56,510 --> 00:42:01,147
I thought about stocking up on milk.

950
00:42:01,715 --> 00:42:04,216
Then again,
who knows what happens tomorrow?

951
00:42:04,217 --> 00:42:06,853
Blowing 500 dollars feels reckless.

952
00:42:06,854 --> 00:42:08,421
- Let's save.
- Sounds good.

953
00:42:08,422 --> 00:42:10,423
What do you think of this order?

954
00:42:10,524 --> 00:42:12,158
If we let the ramyeon soak and expand,

955
00:42:12,159 --> 00:42:13,493
we can stretch it to feed more people.

956
00:42:14,461 --> 00:42:16,228
Look at us, so pitiful.

957
00:42:17,531 --> 00:42:19,665
Four cartons of milk, basic ingredients,

958
00:42:19,767 --> 00:42:21,468
ramyeon, and a loaf of bread.

959
00:42:21,669 --> 00:42:22,669
Looks good.

960
00:42:23,003 --> 00:42:24,570
Purchase confirmed.

961
00:42:24,705 --> 00:42:26,239
The funds will be deducted
from the communal balance.

962
00:42:29,176 --> 00:42:30,510
If I were the spy,

963
00:42:30,511 --> 00:42:31,978
I wouldn't bother targeting myself.

964
00:42:32,613 --> 00:42:34,647
My score is high, making me an easy kill.

965
00:42:35,349 --> 00:42:37,483
Still, we have to look
at the bigger picture.

966
00:42:37,484 --> 00:42:38,985
Isn't today the final Ideology Check?

967
00:42:38,986 --> 00:42:39,952
Right. The last one.

968
00:42:39,953 --> 00:42:41,854
If I get hit today,

969
00:42:41,855 --> 00:42:43,323
can you talk it out...

970
00:42:43,591 --> 00:42:44,758
and protect me?

971
00:42:46,193 --> 00:42:48,761
(Genie, Former leader of Day One,
Immunity Holder)

972
00:42:48,929 --> 00:42:50,730
I'm terrified right now.

973
00:42:51,332 --> 00:42:53,834
- What scares you the most?
- That I might get eliminated.

974
00:42:53,835 --> 00:42:56,703
- But why?
- Well, to start...

975
00:42:56,704 --> 00:42:58,204
she has no immunity.

976
00:42:58,539 --> 00:43:00,740
Second, her score sits at 11.

977
00:43:00,741 --> 00:43:04,177
So she's already in danger.

978
00:43:04,311 --> 00:43:06,178
On top of that, she came out swinging...

979
00:43:06,847 --> 00:43:08,614
- pretty aggressively today.
- True.

980
00:43:08,983 --> 00:43:10,083
Then again...

981
00:43:10,384 --> 00:43:13,186
I always try to look at it
from the spy's point of view.

982
00:43:13,554 --> 00:43:14,587
If I were in their shoes,

983
00:43:14,588 --> 00:43:17,024
I'd see her as a real headache
down the road.

984
00:43:17,025 --> 00:43:18,358
That's a possible way of thinking.

985
00:43:18,359 --> 00:43:20,894
In my case, right from the start,

986
00:43:21,128 --> 00:43:23,596
I made it clear I was hunting the spy.

987
00:43:23,597 --> 00:43:26,065
So the spy has probably
already looked into me.

988
00:43:26,600 --> 00:43:29,168
People like us naturally...

989
00:43:29,503 --> 00:43:31,638
- become their first targets.
- Absolutely.

990
00:43:31,639 --> 00:43:32,872
To nip problems in the bud.

991
00:43:33,007 --> 00:43:35,074
We're bound to be thorns in their side.

992
00:43:36,277 --> 00:43:37,744
I really want to step up from here on out.

993
00:43:38,045 --> 00:43:39,979
Leave the spy hunting to me.

994
00:43:40,114 --> 00:43:41,113
I'm having a blast with this.

995
00:43:43,083 --> 00:43:44,116
Hippo's acting strange.

996
00:43:44,117 --> 00:43:44,984
Totally.

997
00:43:44,985 --> 00:43:47,119
She's especially strange today.

998
00:43:47,120 --> 00:43:49,021
It feels like she's going around
planting seeds of doubt.

999
00:43:54,461 --> 00:43:57,797
Hippo looked the most suspicious today.

1000
00:43:57,998 --> 00:44:00,299
All of a sudden, she started talking...

1001
00:44:00,300 --> 00:44:02,401
really aggressively about the spy.

1002
00:44:02,402 --> 00:44:06,238
Running around stirring
the pot like that seemed off.

1003
00:44:06,573 --> 00:44:07,373
Why do that now?

1004
00:44:07,374 --> 00:44:08,641
All she has to do is make it
through today.

1005
00:44:09,343 --> 00:44:11,277
Why get so aggressive all of a sudden?

1006
00:44:11,278 --> 00:44:13,946
What if she's the spy with a code in hand,

1007
00:44:14,248 --> 00:44:17,951
can't find a way to use it,
and is drumming this up as cover?

1008
00:44:17,952 --> 00:44:19,519
Could it be something like that?

1009
00:44:19,520 --> 00:44:22,255
It felt very suspicious.

1010
00:44:29,930 --> 00:44:32,932
Attention, residents.
An announcement from the Community Center.

1011
00:44:34,535 --> 00:44:37,470
Leader, please report
to the Community Center immediately...

1012
00:44:37,638 --> 00:44:42,241
to collect the rule sheet for
tonight's event that will begin shortly.

1013
00:44:42,443 --> 00:44:43,810
Here it comes.

1014
00:44:44,011 --> 00:44:46,112
I'm getting anxious.

1015
00:44:46,113 --> 00:44:47,413
I'm scared.

1016
00:44:50,985 --> 00:44:52,218
Unbelievable.

1017
00:45:12,606 --> 00:45:15,474
Attention, residents.
An announcement from the Community Center.

1018
00:45:17,945 --> 00:45:19,579
Starting today...

1019
00:45:19,847 --> 00:45:22,081
there will be a daily event...

1020
00:45:22,082 --> 00:45:24,184
that ends in an eviction.

1021
00:45:28,689 --> 00:45:29,689
Today's event is...

1022
00:45:30,157 --> 00:45:32,725
the Ideology Code Deduction Game.

1023
00:45:32,726 --> 00:45:34,060
(Ideology Code Deduction Game)

1024
00:45:36,830 --> 00:45:38,230
It's finally happening.

1025
00:45:38,231 --> 00:45:41,600
We really might have to send someone home.

1026
00:45:41,969 --> 00:45:44,370
Our peace is officially over.

1027
00:45:44,772 --> 00:45:47,574
Now someone actually has to go.

1028
00:45:48,609 --> 00:45:49,576
The game is on.

1029
00:45:51,145 --> 00:45:54,380
Here are the rules
for the Code Deduction Game.

1030
00:45:56,217 --> 00:45:58,183
The Ideology Code Deduction Game...

1031
00:45:58,619 --> 00:46:00,720
marks the final ideology event...

1032
00:46:00,855 --> 00:46:04,156
before Ideology Checks come to an end.

1033
00:46:05,893 --> 00:46:07,795
"The Ideology Code Deduction Game..."

1034
00:46:07,796 --> 00:46:11,130
"consists of three rounds, one per hour."

1035
00:46:11,565 --> 00:46:14,433
At the start of the game,
every resident will receive...

1036
00:46:14,801 --> 00:46:17,403
one bonus attack token.

1037
00:46:17,404 --> 00:46:18,905
(Bonus attack token)

1038
00:46:19,440 --> 00:46:22,175
"With this bonus attack token,"

1039
00:46:22,543 --> 00:46:26,279
"no personal funds will be deducted
for failure or nonuse."

1040
00:46:28,515 --> 00:46:31,083
Throughout the game, any resident...

1041
00:46:31,285 --> 00:46:34,020
may initiate an Ideology Check
at any time.

1042
00:46:34,021 --> 00:46:35,089
(Ideology Check)

1043
00:46:35,090 --> 00:46:37,624
Once the bonus token is used,

1044
00:46:38,393 --> 00:46:40,593
additional attack tokens may
be purchased...

1045
00:46:40,794 --> 00:46:42,995
for 1,000 dollars each...

1046
00:46:43,230 --> 00:46:46,099
with no limit.

1047
00:46:49,236 --> 00:46:50,269
"No limit."

1048
00:46:50,472 --> 00:46:52,071
At the start of each round,

1049
00:46:52,306 --> 00:46:54,841
the leader must report
to the Center within five minutes...

1050
00:46:55,309 --> 00:46:57,409
to set the resident turn order.

1051
00:46:59,513 --> 00:47:00,913
Once the order is set,

1052
00:47:01,081 --> 00:47:03,582
residents will enter the Center
one by one...

1053
00:47:04,084 --> 00:47:06,586
to check the combined code score
of themselves...

1054
00:47:06,587 --> 00:47:08,687
and one other resident of their choice.

1055
00:47:09,923 --> 00:47:11,790
"The combined code score reflects..."

1056
00:47:11,791 --> 00:47:13,592
"the sum of two residents' scores."

1057
00:47:14,328 --> 00:47:17,463
If their codes lean
in opposite directions,

1058
00:47:17,831 --> 00:47:19,965
the scores are combined in full.

1059
00:47:19,966 --> 00:47:21,167
(All scores combined.)

1060
00:47:21,168 --> 00:47:23,068
(Total score: 18)

1061
00:47:23,069 --> 00:47:26,105
If their codes lean in the same direction,

1062
00:47:26,240 --> 00:47:28,607
only the higher score is counted.

1063
00:47:28,608 --> 00:47:29,775
(Higher score only)

1064
00:47:29,776 --> 00:47:32,378
(Total score: 10)

1065
00:47:32,813 --> 00:47:35,848
"Once all 13 residents have taken
their turns,"

1066
00:47:36,316 --> 00:47:39,285
"the total number of Ideology Checks..."

1067
00:47:39,453 --> 00:47:41,554
"and their outcomes will be announced."

1068
00:47:43,924 --> 00:47:46,125
If an Ideology Check succeeds,

1069
00:47:46,727 --> 00:47:49,962
the targeted resident becomes a casualty.

1070
00:47:50,497 --> 00:47:52,298
The casualty's entire prize fund...

1071
00:47:52,299 --> 00:47:54,767
is transferred to the attacker.

1072
00:47:54,768 --> 00:47:56,535
(Check successful.)

1073
00:47:56,536 --> 00:47:58,104
A resident who is already a casualty...

1074
00:47:58,305 --> 00:48:00,239
cannot attack another resident.

1075
00:48:01,141 --> 00:48:03,074
If someone attacks...

1076
00:48:03,075 --> 00:48:05,411
a resident who is already a casualty,

1077
00:48:05,846 --> 00:48:09,916
the attempt is void and the token
is refunded.

1078
00:48:10,752 --> 00:48:12,218
Any resident who becomes a casualty...

1079
00:48:12,486 --> 00:48:16,055
will be evicted immediately following
the conclusion of the Code Deduction Game.

1080
00:48:16,456 --> 00:48:18,857
"If a casualty holds immunity..."

1081
00:48:18,858 --> 00:48:21,360
"before the game concludes,"

1082
00:48:21,495 --> 00:48:23,463
"only their prize money is transferred."

1083
00:48:23,830 --> 00:48:25,531
"They will avoid eviction."

1084
00:48:25,933 --> 00:48:27,934
"Their immunity will then expire."

1085
00:48:29,469 --> 00:48:31,103
"To transfer immunity,"

1086
00:48:31,104 --> 00:48:33,539
"both the grantor and the recipient..."

1087
00:48:33,540 --> 00:48:36,375
"must visit the Center together."

1088
00:48:38,378 --> 00:48:42,147
"If no one is evicted
during the Code Deduction Game,"

1089
00:48:42,382 --> 00:48:44,016
"a sudden-death round will take place."

1090
00:48:44,218 --> 00:48:45,151
There's no avoiding it.

1091
00:48:45,987 --> 00:48:48,321
So someone's definitely leaving today?

1092
00:48:48,322 --> 00:48:50,756
The biggest difference from yesterday...

1093
00:48:50,757 --> 00:48:54,559
is that the bedroom screen won't show...

1094
00:48:54,560 --> 00:48:57,129
attacks or outcomes during the match.

1095
00:48:57,497 --> 00:48:59,865
That might not change much.

1096
00:48:59,866 --> 00:49:02,635
Still, triggering another match
if nobody gets evicted...

1097
00:49:02,636 --> 00:49:04,570
is the biggest gamble
they've thrown at us.

1098
00:49:04,571 --> 00:49:05,571
- Right.
- That's how I read it.

1099
00:49:05,973 --> 00:49:09,509
They're daring us to see if we'll band
together not to eliminate anyone...

1100
00:49:09,510 --> 00:49:12,011
and take our chances
with whatever nightmare comes next.

1101
00:49:13,046 --> 00:49:15,381
Or just sweat out three hours
to secure our safety.

1102
00:49:15,382 --> 00:49:16,648
That might be the real test.

1103
00:49:17,551 --> 00:49:18,918
In plain terms,

1104
00:49:19,019 --> 00:49:21,821
someone is definitely getting eliminated.

1105
00:49:22,155 --> 00:49:25,524
Our best move would be...

1106
00:49:25,626 --> 00:49:26,960
figuring out who the spy is.

1107
00:49:26,961 --> 00:49:29,062
That would be ideal.

1108
00:49:29,063 --> 00:49:32,098
If someone has to go regardless,

1109
00:49:32,099 --> 00:49:35,168
we might as well take out someone...

1110
00:49:35,169 --> 00:49:36,836
who genuinely looks like the spy.

1111
00:49:36,837 --> 00:49:38,237
At least then we'd have a good reason.

1112
00:49:38,238 --> 00:49:40,639
If we play blindly...

1113
00:49:40,640 --> 00:49:43,676
and an innocent person goes down,

1114
00:49:43,677 --> 00:49:46,079
nobody will ever trust anyone again.

1115
00:49:46,080 --> 00:49:49,048
It'll turn into a total bloodbath.

1116
00:49:49,049 --> 00:49:50,850
We have to stick together.

1117
00:49:50,851 --> 00:49:54,422
Even if we guess wrong,

1118
00:49:54,423 --> 00:49:58,291
it's the only way to keep us from falling
into every-man-for-himself chaos.

1119
00:49:58,292 --> 00:50:00,127
I really think that's our only move.

1120
00:50:00,128 --> 00:50:02,061
Assuming an eviction is guaranteed.

1121
00:50:03,530 --> 00:50:04,763
So you're saying we combine our forces...

1122
00:50:04,764 --> 00:50:06,232
and all focus on a single target.

1123
00:50:06,233 --> 00:50:07,066
Exactly.

1124
00:50:08,602 --> 00:50:10,836
Because in this game,

1125
00:50:10,837 --> 00:50:13,372
the spy holds all the cards.

1126
00:50:13,373 --> 00:50:16,509
- True.
- They already know the codes...

1127
00:50:16,510 --> 00:50:18,477
of whoever they scoped out.

1128
00:50:18,478 --> 00:50:21,647
They could take them out in a heartbeat.

1129
00:50:21,648 --> 00:50:23,282
Should we have just taken the money?

1130
00:50:23,283 --> 00:50:26,686
There's a clean way to win this.

1131
00:50:26,687 --> 00:50:29,889
All we have to do is pinpoint the spy.

1132
00:50:29,890 --> 00:50:32,825
The spy is bound to use a code
they've already seen.

1133
00:50:32,826 --> 00:50:35,861
That narrows the field.

1134
00:50:35,862 --> 00:50:37,832
If we all agree not to attack today?

1135
00:50:37,833 --> 00:50:39,865
Then we'll see who the spy went after.

1136
00:50:39,866 --> 00:50:41,100
We'll spot the victim right away.

1137
00:50:41,101 --> 00:50:42,401
- And then protect them?
- Exactly.

1138
00:50:43,203 --> 00:50:44,770
(Genie, Day One leader with immunity)

1139
00:50:44,771 --> 00:50:47,039
(Benjamin, Day Three leader with immunity)

1140
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:48,541
(Go Ae Shin,
Day Four leader with immunity)

1141
00:50:48,542 --> 00:50:49,909
(Polar Bear, Day Two leader with immunity)

1142
00:50:49,910 --> 00:50:51,277
Then again...

1143
00:50:51,278 --> 00:50:52,778
like I said,
that relies on one big assumption.

1144
00:50:52,779 --> 00:50:54,446
If we protect those three,

1145
00:50:54,447 --> 00:50:55,648
and nobody gets evicted...

1146
00:50:55,649 --> 00:50:57,249
after three rounds,

1147
00:50:57,250 --> 00:50:59,585
- Right.
- we're forced to roll the dice...

1148
00:50:59,586 --> 00:51:01,187
on the next game.

1149
00:51:01,421 --> 00:51:03,589
It falls apart unless every single person
is on board.

1150
00:51:03,590 --> 00:51:04,823
Still, this is...

1151
00:51:04,824 --> 00:51:06,792
the final Ideology Check game.

1152
00:51:06,793 --> 00:51:09,195
The point I really want to make is...

1153
00:51:09,196 --> 00:51:10,596
we can't just sit back and play defense.

1154
00:51:10,597 --> 00:51:12,898
Even if it means taking some risks,

1155
00:51:12,899 --> 00:51:15,168
it's time we figure out a sharp way...

1156
00:51:15,169 --> 00:51:17,403
to strike first.

1157
00:51:18,638 --> 00:51:20,240
- Honestly...
- We did talk about this.

1158
00:51:20,241 --> 00:51:21,610
Maybe the time has come to push forward.

1159
00:51:21,611 --> 00:51:23,642
- Could be.
- I really think it has.

1160
00:51:23,643 --> 00:51:27,079
"Every round, the leader has
five minutes to reach the Center..."

1161
00:51:27,080 --> 00:51:29,014
"and set the lineup."

1162
00:51:29,249 --> 00:51:30,649
That's what the rule says.

1163
00:51:30,917 --> 00:51:32,784
The spy has already seen someone's code.

1164
00:51:32,785 --> 00:51:35,621
We just don't know whose.

1165
00:51:35,622 --> 00:51:36,788
So the turn order...

1166
00:51:37,591 --> 00:51:39,425
In reality, this means...

1167
00:51:39,426 --> 00:51:41,494
going early puts you
at a total disadvantage.

1168
00:51:42,329 --> 00:51:43,128
Right.

1169
00:51:43,129 --> 00:51:45,898
You could finish your turn
without touching anyone,

1170
00:51:45,899 --> 00:51:47,066
only to get taken out
by someone behind you,

1171
00:51:47,067 --> 00:51:48,300
leaving you with zero chance to counter.

1172
00:51:48,568 --> 00:51:51,403
- Going late gives you the upper hand.
- Exactly.

1173
00:51:54,274 --> 00:51:57,276
(Ten minutes before the game)

1174
00:51:57,277 --> 00:52:01,080
Round One is everything.

1175
00:52:01,081 --> 00:52:02,848
If we get lucky enough...

1176
00:52:04,518 --> 00:52:07,787
to catch the spy in a single move,

1177
00:52:08,889 --> 00:52:10,456
it practically solves everything.

1178
00:52:12,058 --> 00:52:16,561
A setup like this just crushes idealism.

1179
00:52:17,832 --> 00:52:18,798
We're backed into a corner.

1180
00:52:19,766 --> 00:52:20,666
Four.

1181
00:52:21,268 --> 00:52:22,768
Four. Mine is four as well.

1182
00:52:25,739 --> 00:52:27,339
Dark Knight is a really tough read.

1183
00:52:29,676 --> 00:52:31,276
But Hippo is suspicious to me.

1184
00:52:35,282 --> 00:52:37,283
Push the suspects to the back of the line.

1185
00:52:38,285 --> 00:52:39,718
I honestly have no clue.

1186
00:52:41,555 --> 00:52:45,391
Checking their score against mine
would give it away fast.

1187
00:52:46,126 --> 00:52:47,726
Say this is their score.

1188
00:52:49,463 --> 00:52:52,331
Then I know for sure my score here is one.

1189
00:52:53,166 --> 00:52:54,666
And this one is one, too.

1190
00:52:56,137 --> 00:52:57,837
Then I can definitely finish them off.

1191
00:53:01,942 --> 00:53:04,544
Adding them up hands me a clear answer.

1192
00:53:04,545 --> 00:53:05,511
It's a wrap.

1193
00:53:06,847 --> 00:53:08,381
Five and five.

1194
00:53:09,416 --> 00:53:10,750
Two tries ought to do it.

1195
00:53:11,752 --> 00:53:13,753
Time to keep a straight face.

1196
00:53:13,954 --> 00:53:15,821
I've got no choice but to bluff.

1197
00:53:16,723 --> 00:53:20,359
(Ideology Code Deduction Game)

1198
00:53:21,795 --> 00:53:24,229
This game is ridiculous.

1199
00:53:24,530 --> 00:53:27,266
It's completely cutthroat.

1200
00:53:27,435 --> 00:53:29,268
Well, they said attacking isn't mandatory.

1201
00:53:29,503 --> 00:53:30,470
Then let's just hold fire.

1202
00:53:31,004 --> 00:53:32,538
We don't have to attack.

1203
00:53:33,039 --> 00:53:34,696
Except it doesn't end
until someone gets evicted.

1204
00:53:34,697 --> 00:53:37,410
The messed-up part is,
even if none of us attack,

1205
00:53:37,411 --> 00:53:40,045
the spy might still pull the trigger.

1206
00:53:40,046 --> 00:53:41,146
Who could it be?

1207
00:53:41,514 --> 00:53:43,549
Why put us through this misery?

1208
00:53:45,418 --> 00:53:49,087
I still can't wrap my head around
the fact that one of us is a spy.

1209
00:53:50,690 --> 00:53:53,792
Attention, residents.
An announcement from the Community Center.

1210
00:53:54,194 --> 00:53:57,530
The leader, please report
to the Center within five minutes...

1211
00:53:57,698 --> 00:53:59,765
to set the order.

1212
00:54:00,267 --> 00:54:01,266
(Round One order)

1213
00:54:01,267 --> 00:54:02,467
Set the lineup quickly.

1214
00:54:04,371 --> 00:54:06,605
Though in this situation, the order...

1215
00:54:06,606 --> 00:54:08,307
- hardly matters.
- Doesn't matter much.

1216
00:54:08,742 --> 00:54:10,309
It changes nothing.

1217
00:54:10,310 --> 00:54:11,677
(Michael disapproves of their mindset.)

1218
00:54:12,178 --> 00:54:13,879
What genuinely worries me is...

1219
00:54:13,880 --> 00:54:16,247
if we keep playing like this,

1220
00:54:16,248 --> 00:54:17,749
it's going to turn into a bloodbath.

1221
00:54:20,387 --> 00:54:23,689
Going in without any plan whatsoever?

1222
00:54:23,690 --> 00:54:24,957
I don't think that's the answer.

1223
00:54:25,893 --> 00:54:28,060
The lineup, at the very least,

1224
00:54:28,395 --> 00:54:30,028
needs some kind of reasoning behind it.

1225
00:54:32,532 --> 00:54:34,500
How about this?

1226
00:54:34,734 --> 00:54:36,368
If someone runs extra checks,

1227
00:54:36,369 --> 00:54:38,203
we'll catch it on the clock.

1228
00:54:38,771 --> 00:54:42,174
Taking longer means burning
another token and waiting on the result.

1229
00:54:42,175 --> 00:54:43,676
Then they come out.

1230
00:54:43,910 --> 00:54:46,678
Let's all just get in and out
as fast as possible.

1231
00:54:46,679 --> 00:54:47,713
Sounds good.

1232
00:54:47,714 --> 00:54:49,715
- Simple as that. Problem solved.
- Great.

1233
00:54:49,716 --> 00:54:50,817
But...

1234
00:54:50,818 --> 00:54:52,385
That's just doing the same old thing.

1235
00:54:52,386 --> 00:54:53,820
It brings us right back to square one.

1236
00:54:53,821 --> 00:54:55,655
Are you trying to ensure no one leaves?

1237
00:54:55,656 --> 00:54:56,989
So are we taking the gamble or not?

1238
00:54:56,990 --> 00:54:59,691
We can pull this off
for rounds one and two.

1239
00:55:00,360 --> 00:55:03,329
Worst-case scenario,
we end up in that tiebreaker game...

1240
00:55:03,330 --> 00:55:04,496
after all that effort...

1241
00:55:04,497 --> 00:55:06,699
and still lose someone, right?

1242
00:55:06,700 --> 00:55:08,133
Then we just use one immunity...

1243
00:55:08,134 --> 00:55:09,702
to save them.

1244
00:55:09,703 --> 00:55:11,103
For instance, right when it starts,

1245
00:55:11,104 --> 00:55:13,872
let's agree that anyone taking over
a minute is automatically the spy.

1246
00:55:13,873 --> 00:55:14,807
Let's run it like that.

1247
00:55:14,808 --> 00:55:17,109
If you are anxious,
you can just jot down the number.

1248
00:55:17,110 --> 00:55:18,243
Works for me.

1249
00:55:18,244 --> 00:55:19,411
Good. I'm in.

1250
00:55:20,113 --> 00:55:22,147
I have one proposal for Round One.

1251
00:55:22,148 --> 00:55:24,016
If you suspect someone on your own...

1252
00:55:24,017 --> 00:55:26,485
and want to take a swing,

1253
00:55:26,486 --> 00:55:28,620
could you please hold off
just for this round?

1254
00:55:28,621 --> 00:55:29,222
Agreed.

1255
00:55:29,223 --> 00:55:30,522
That gives us a chance
to piece things together.

1256
00:55:30,757 --> 00:55:33,325
If one of us attacks on our own,

1257
00:55:33,660 --> 00:55:36,328
that move gets tangled up
with whatever the spy does.

1258
00:55:36,329 --> 00:55:37,663
Then we'll have no way to trace it.

1259
00:55:37,664 --> 00:55:42,134
In Round One, nobody attacks
except the spy.

1260
00:55:42,135 --> 00:55:43,269
- Right.
- Count me in.

1261
00:55:43,903 --> 00:55:46,939
They're making us pick between goodwill,
teaming up, or sheer chaos.

1262
00:55:46,940 --> 00:55:47,973
One of the three.

1263
00:55:49,309 --> 00:55:51,577
I was hoping to cruise
through two or three days,

1264
00:55:51,578 --> 00:55:53,979
mess with them a bit,
and slip away on the final day.

1265
00:55:53,980 --> 00:55:55,914
Things aren't playing out my way, though.

1266
00:55:55,915 --> 00:55:57,216
They aren't letting me skate by.

1267
00:55:57,418 --> 00:55:58,951
It was pretty frustrating.

1268
00:55:59,552 --> 00:56:02,554
(Setting the turn order for Round One)

1269
00:56:07,794 --> 00:56:09,795
(No. 1: Dark Knight)

1270
00:56:09,796 --> 00:56:12,264
The one who made a false statement...

1271
00:56:12,332 --> 00:56:13,699
was Dark Knight.

1272
00:56:15,502 --> 00:56:17,169
(No. 2: Hippo)

1273
00:56:17,170 --> 00:56:18,771
- Hippo is acting strange.
- Totally.

1274
00:56:19,105 --> 00:56:21,039
It's like she's going around
stirring up doubt.

1275
00:56:21,441 --> 00:56:24,607
(Round One: 1. Dark Knight,
2. Hippo, 3. Nangja)

1276
00:56:24,608 --> 00:56:27,742
(4. Ted, 5. Go Ae Shin, 6. Michael,
7. Genie, 8. Superman)

1277
00:56:27,743 --> 00:56:30,949
(9. Sugar, 10. Gray, 11. Benjamin,
12. Banu, 13. Polar Bear)

1278
00:56:31,151 --> 00:56:33,219
Round One begins now.

1279
00:56:33,220 --> 00:56:34,286
(Code Game: Round One)

1280
00:56:34,554 --> 00:56:35,854
Resident Dark Knight,

1281
00:56:36,322 --> 00:56:39,858
please proceed to the Community Center.

1282
00:56:40,326 --> 00:56:42,027
Let's time this. Go.

1283
00:56:42,028 --> 00:56:43,729
Let's see how long it takes...

1284
00:56:43,730 --> 00:56:45,163
- just to check the number.
- Just the score.

1285
00:56:45,164 --> 00:56:46,631
(Ideology Code Game: Round One)

1286
00:56:57,777 --> 00:56:58,644
(Select an action.)

1287
00:56:58,645 --> 00:57:00,045
(1. Check Score, 2. Attack, 3. Transfer)

1288
00:57:00,313 --> 00:57:01,713
Combined score check.

1289
00:57:02,015 --> 00:57:03,282
(Enter name for combined score.)

1290
00:57:03,283 --> 00:57:04,016
All right.

1291
00:57:04,384 --> 00:57:06,452
(Hippo)

1292
00:57:06,453 --> 00:57:08,053
(Dark Knight checks his score with Hippo.)

1293
00:57:08,054 --> 00:57:08,854
Hippo.

1294
00:57:10,857 --> 00:57:13,992
Now that I think about it,
Hippo is really...

1295
00:57:13,993 --> 00:57:16,061
She's turning into the next Michael.

1296
00:57:16,062 --> 00:57:18,263
Totally obsessed with the spy.

1297
00:57:19,632 --> 00:57:22,300
(Combined score check with Hippo)

1298
00:57:22,301 --> 00:57:23,657
(L3, R2, Total 5)

1299
00:57:23,658 --> 00:57:24,603
(F3, E2, Total 5)

1300
00:57:24,604 --> 00:57:25,471
(W3, U0, Total 3)

1301
00:57:25,472 --> 00:57:26,371
(O2, C1, Total 4)

1302
00:57:26,372 --> 00:57:29,240
(Total Score: 17)

1303
00:57:29,876 --> 00:57:30,676
Got it.

1304
00:57:37,917 --> 00:57:39,384
All set.

1305
00:57:39,385 --> 00:57:42,354
Attention, residents.
An announcement from the Community Center.

1306
00:57:43,022 --> 00:57:45,523
Resident Hippo,

1307
00:57:45,524 --> 00:57:49,060
please proceed to the Community Center.

1308
00:57:49,061 --> 00:57:51,997
Walking at a brisk pace,
it should take around two minutes.

1309
00:57:53,067 --> 00:57:54,967
Pretty clever angle.

1310
00:57:54,968 --> 00:57:56,803
What should we do for Round Two?

1311
00:57:56,804 --> 00:57:58,504
We can keep this up through Round Two.

1312
00:57:58,505 --> 00:58:00,841
That way, going into Round Three,
we only face one casualty.

1313
00:58:00,842 --> 00:58:02,641
Just one, no matter what happens.

1314
00:58:06,513 --> 00:58:09,615
I'll go with the combined score check.

1315
00:58:12,619 --> 00:58:16,255
(Superman)

1316
00:58:16,256 --> 00:58:19,191
I checked my combined score with Superman.

1317
00:58:19,559 --> 00:58:21,793
The system gives you more insight...

1318
00:58:21,794 --> 00:58:24,663
when you pick someone with opposing views.

1319
00:58:24,664 --> 00:58:28,033
So I went with Superman,
who seemed furthest from me.

1320
00:58:28,501 --> 00:58:31,036
(Combined score check with Superman)

1321
00:58:31,571 --> 00:58:32,639
(L3, R2, Total 5)

1322
00:58:32,640 --> 00:58:33,438
(F3, E2, Total 5)

1323
00:58:33,439 --> 00:58:34,207
(W2, U2, Total 4)

1324
00:58:34,208 --> 00:58:35,274
(O3, C1, Total 4)

1325
00:58:35,275 --> 00:58:39,845
(Total Score: 18)

1326
00:58:39,846 --> 00:58:42,514
I toyed with the idea of attacking him.

1327
00:58:42,515 --> 00:58:45,083
Then again, taking a shot...

1328
00:58:45,084 --> 00:58:47,853
would have been dead obvious
under these conditions.

1329
00:58:47,854 --> 00:58:50,923
Just checking his score was
the furthest I could go to cover myself.

1330
00:58:53,193 --> 00:58:55,396
(Nangja checks her score with Benjamin.)

1331
00:58:55,397 --> 00:58:57,963
I wanted the leverage
to take aim at Benjamin...

1332
00:58:57,964 --> 00:59:01,433
whenever I needed to,
so I pulled his code.

1333
00:59:01,434 --> 00:59:03,736
(Nangja and Benjamin's combined score)

1334
00:59:04,304 --> 00:59:05,704
(L0, R1, Total 1, F0, E2, Total 2)

1335
00:59:05,705 --> 00:59:07,373
(W1, U0, Total 1, O1, C1, Total 2)

1336
00:59:07,740 --> 00:59:08,941
(Ted checks with Gray.)

1337
00:59:08,942 --> 00:59:10,408
I went with Gray.

1338
00:59:10,409 --> 00:59:12,511
It felt like Gray's attitude...

1339
00:59:12,512 --> 00:59:13,947
shifted a bit...

1340
00:59:14,180 --> 00:59:14,813
today.

1341
00:59:15,181 --> 00:59:17,082
(Ted and Gray's combined code score)

1342
00:59:17,083 --> 00:59:19,217
(Total score: 9)

1343
00:59:19,652 --> 00:59:21,353
(Gray checks his score with Benjamin.)

1344
00:59:21,354 --> 00:59:22,988
(Gray and Benjamin's combined score)

1345
00:59:24,023 --> 00:59:25,624
(Total Score: 11)

1346
00:59:25,792 --> 00:59:27,893
(Genie checks her score with Hippo.)

1347
00:59:27,894 --> 00:59:29,495
(Genie and Hippo's combined code score)

1348
00:59:30,363 --> 00:59:31,964
(Total Score: 17)

1349
00:59:32,432 --> 00:59:34,733
(Superman checks his score with Benjamin.)

1350
00:59:34,734 --> 00:59:36,568
(Superman and Benjamin's combined score)

1351
00:59:37,070 --> 00:59:39,104
(Total Score: 9)

1352
00:59:39,572 --> 00:59:41,873
(Benjamin, 11th in line)

1353
00:59:44,510 --> 00:59:45,377
Instead of that,

1354
00:59:45,378 --> 00:59:47,312
can I see Ted's complete code profile?

1355
00:59:48,581 --> 00:59:49,915
Ted's full code lookup.

1356
00:59:49,916 --> 00:59:50,982
I'm the spy.

1357
00:59:52,085 --> 00:59:54,487
Once I'm in, I'll knock both out fast.

1358
00:59:54,488 --> 00:59:56,455
I'll probably have to make my move
in Round Three.

1359
00:59:56,990 --> 00:59:59,391
Otherwise, this game will drag on forever.

1360
00:59:59,791 --> 01:00:01,593
I felt like we had to look out
for the Reporter.

1361
01:00:01,894 --> 01:00:04,262
It wouldn't sit right with me
if the Reporter got eliminated.

1362
01:00:04,497 --> 01:00:05,931
To stop that from happening,

1363
01:00:05,932 --> 01:00:08,300
someone has to take the hit
and wrap this up.

1364
01:00:12,338 --> 01:00:13,205
All right.

1365
01:00:14,308 --> 01:00:16,075
I'll go with Option One.

1366
01:00:16,376 --> 01:00:19,478
(After checking the full code,
Benjamin checks a combined score.)

1367
01:00:19,479 --> 01:00:20,279
Hippo.

1368
01:00:20,280 --> 01:00:21,080
(Hippo)

1369
01:00:21,081 --> 01:00:22,081
(Combined code score is...)

1370
01:00:22,082 --> 01:00:22,982
(13 points)

1371
01:00:23,248 --> 01:00:24,415
All right, I'm done.

1372
01:00:29,122 --> 01:00:32,492
All 13 residents have
completed their checks.

1373
01:00:32,493 --> 01:00:33,425
Already?

1374
01:00:33,426 --> 01:00:36,762
Across all 13 visits, the number
of Ideology Checks was...

1375
01:00:38,431 --> 01:00:40,565
zero.

1376
01:00:41,534 --> 01:00:45,337
There were zero successful checks.

1377
01:00:46,406 --> 01:00:47,306
The spy didn't make a move.

1378
01:00:47,307 --> 01:00:50,843
You are now free to move about.

1379
01:00:51,010 --> 01:00:52,544
You may confirm your status...

1380
01:00:52,545 --> 01:00:55,547
at the Community Center.

1381
01:00:55,748 --> 01:00:56,648
Why didn't they attack?

1382
01:00:56,983 --> 01:00:58,784
They might be holding out for Round Three.

1383
01:00:58,785 --> 01:01:00,152
Everyone moved fast earlier.

1384
01:01:00,420 --> 01:01:01,453
Caught them off guard, maybe.

1385
01:01:01,454 --> 01:01:02,558
They played it safe...

1386
01:01:02,559 --> 01:01:04,155
- to avoid suspicion this round.
- Could be.

1387
01:01:04,156 --> 01:01:06,291
They could just blitz three attacks
in Round Three.

1388
01:01:06,292 --> 01:01:08,460
Can't do that.
It's capped at one per round.

1389
01:01:08,461 --> 01:01:10,395
Wait, the rules say...

1390
01:01:10,396 --> 01:01:11,830
"During the game,"

1391
01:01:11,831 --> 01:01:14,432
"you can trigger an Ideology Check
at any time."

1392
01:01:14,433 --> 01:01:17,202
"At any time."
That's literally what it says.

1393
01:01:17,203 --> 01:01:20,705
They could sneak back in later.

1394
01:01:20,706 --> 01:01:23,341
- Right.
- Not while everyone's watching, though.

1395
01:01:23,342 --> 01:01:25,110
Still, here's the catch.

1396
01:01:25,111 --> 01:01:27,212
They could stroll in pretending
to check their status...

1397
01:01:27,213 --> 01:01:29,013
and launch a sudden strike.

1398
01:01:30,316 --> 01:01:31,583
That's definitely on the table.

1399
01:01:31,584 --> 01:01:34,052
So our real goal...

1400
01:01:34,053 --> 01:01:35,654
is to keep that tally at zero...

1401
01:01:36,055 --> 01:01:37,622
and make sure nobody gets left behind.

1402
01:01:37,623 --> 01:01:38,923
If someone gets evicted,

1403
01:01:38,924 --> 01:01:40,458
only 12 of the 13 of us...

1404
01:01:40,459 --> 01:01:42,360
walk out of here today.

1405
01:01:44,163 --> 01:01:45,797
There might still be a way out
where everyone stays.

1406
01:01:45,900 --> 01:01:48,200
The next game could really...

1407
01:01:51,037 --> 01:01:52,771
About that awkward truth...

1408
01:01:52,772 --> 01:01:55,640
I'll just put it out there first.

1409
01:01:56,043 --> 01:01:57,776
Ever since Day One,

1410
01:01:57,777 --> 01:02:00,045
I've had my eyes on Gray and Dark Knight.

1411
01:02:00,046 --> 01:02:01,547
I won't pretend otherwise.

1412
01:02:01,548 --> 01:02:04,217
Now we hear Dark Knight...

1413
01:02:04,218 --> 01:02:06,385
claiming it was just an honest mistake.

1414
01:02:06,386 --> 01:02:08,353
Honestly, though...

1415
01:02:08,521 --> 01:02:11,155
tactics and high-level gameplay...

1416
01:02:11,156 --> 01:02:13,591
demand a sharp memory.

1417
01:02:14,393 --> 01:02:17,663
So what really bugs me is this.

1418
01:02:18,064 --> 01:02:19,698
Did he honestly...

1419
01:02:19,866 --> 01:02:22,334
just forget after a single day?

1420
01:02:22,335 --> 01:02:24,803
A player as sharp as Dark Knight?

1421
01:02:25,204 --> 01:02:26,905
That just doesn't add up to me.

1422
01:02:27,106 --> 01:02:29,107
(Michael suspects Dark Knight
of being the spy.)

1423
01:02:29,308 --> 01:02:30,441
Suspicion.

1424
01:02:30,442 --> 01:02:33,177
Fair suspicion, you could call it.

1425
01:02:38,518 --> 01:02:41,220
To be blunt, I doubted Ted at one point.

1426
01:02:41,221 --> 01:02:42,154
Because...

1427
01:02:42,155 --> 01:02:43,455
(Gray suspects Ted.)

1428
01:02:43,589 --> 01:02:46,124
If you want to stay off the radar
as the spy,

1429
01:02:46,125 --> 01:02:49,961
you have to be the person
nobody would ever suspect.

1430
01:02:50,630 --> 01:02:52,797
After yesterday's play...

1431
01:02:52,798 --> 01:02:56,668
everyone was praising Ted so much...

1432
01:02:56,669 --> 01:03:00,405
that he seemed completely untouchable.

1433
01:03:00,406 --> 01:03:02,874
I went up to him a few times...

1434
01:03:02,875 --> 01:03:04,842
trying to pull him into my corner.

1435
01:03:04,843 --> 01:03:07,745
He just said he'd make his call
when the moment came.

1436
01:03:07,746 --> 01:03:08,648
Kept repeating that.

1437
01:03:08,649 --> 01:03:10,214
He stayed right down the middle.

1438
01:03:10,215 --> 01:03:13,084
Which means he refuses to pick a side.

1439
01:03:13,085 --> 01:03:15,353
He needs to keep everybody close.

1440
01:03:15,555 --> 01:03:16,555
And where does that lead?

1441
01:03:16,556 --> 01:03:17,990
Both camps end up coming to him.

1442
01:03:17,991 --> 01:03:19,358
(Ted's neutral stance draws skepticism.)

1443
01:03:19,359 --> 01:03:20,492
Right where he wants to be.

1444
01:03:21,594 --> 01:03:23,328
Either way,

1445
01:03:23,329 --> 01:03:26,298
I figured the spy wouldn't be...

1446
01:03:26,299 --> 01:03:28,233
someone openly stirring up trouble.

1447
01:03:28,234 --> 01:03:30,470
It'd be someone who puts everyone at ease.

1448
01:03:30,471 --> 01:03:34,806
Thinking through the voices in this room,

1449
01:03:34,807 --> 01:03:38,209
I had ruled Ted out completely.

1450
01:03:38,210 --> 01:03:40,645
Flip that logic on its head, though,

1451
01:03:40,646 --> 01:03:43,615
and you realize he fits the profile
perfectly.

1452
01:03:43,616 --> 01:03:45,584
I'm just laying my cards on the table.

1453
01:03:46,986 --> 01:03:48,820
I don't mean any offense by it.

1454
01:03:48,821 --> 01:03:50,855
If we're putting everything on the table,

1455
01:03:51,157 --> 01:03:52,858
I've been keeping an eye on Nangja.

1456
01:03:52,859 --> 01:03:54,427
(Ted suspects Nangja.)

1457
01:03:54,428 --> 01:03:55,427
I haven't taken my eyes off her.

1458
01:03:55,428 --> 01:03:57,096
(This morning)

1459
01:03:57,097 --> 01:04:00,899
I'm still wondering why Nangja broke down
crying back then.

1460
01:04:00,900 --> 01:04:02,367
It's been nagging at me.

1461
01:04:02,368 --> 01:04:05,971
So I figured
I should keep a closer watch on her.

1462
01:04:05,972 --> 01:04:07,038
(Ted agreed with Sugar.)

1463
01:04:09,442 --> 01:04:12,310
Truth is, Gray was my top suspect.

1464
01:04:12,845 --> 01:04:14,546
That's why I went out of my way...

1465
01:04:14,547 --> 01:04:16,182
to rally everyone...

1466
01:04:16,183 --> 01:04:17,982
around asking that question.

1467
01:04:18,451 --> 01:04:22,320
Gray just seemed to be acting awkward too.

1468
01:04:22,755 --> 01:04:25,056
That was my read on it.

1469
01:04:25,258 --> 01:04:26,524
Awkward how?

1470
01:04:27,460 --> 01:04:30,262
I mean...

1471
01:04:32,565 --> 01:04:36,234
I assumed people were finally
done suspecting me.

1472
01:04:36,235 --> 01:04:38,670
Then out of nowhere,
people start calling Gray suspicious.

1473
01:04:38,671 --> 01:04:40,105
It completely threw me off.

1474
01:04:40,406 --> 01:04:42,240
People are finally starting...

1475
01:04:42,241 --> 01:04:44,676
to show their true colors.

1476
01:04:44,745 --> 01:04:46,645
Call out one person you don't trust.

1477
01:04:46,812 --> 01:04:47,746
One after another.

1478
01:04:47,747 --> 01:04:49,747
Everyone has their crosshairs
on someone else.

1479
01:04:49,849 --> 01:04:51,516
Look, Nangja...

1480
01:04:51,517 --> 01:04:53,285
is genuinely sweet and kind.

1481
01:04:53,286 --> 01:04:54,786
Even so, I can't help suspecting her.

1482
01:04:54,787 --> 01:04:57,789
Ted is simply too perceptive.

1483
01:04:57,790 --> 01:04:58,824
That's exactly why he makes me nervous.

1484
01:04:58,825 --> 01:05:00,892
So who's left that you actually trust?

1485
01:05:09,101 --> 01:05:11,569
Round One has concluded.

1486
01:05:12,271 --> 01:05:14,473
During this round, the spy...

1487
01:05:14,474 --> 01:05:17,875
viewed the complete code set
of one resident.

1488
01:05:19,612 --> 01:05:20,779
That brings the count to four.

1489
01:05:20,780 --> 01:05:23,748
(The spy's fourth full code lookup)

1490
01:05:25,918 --> 01:05:28,619
(Round Two order confirmed)

1491
01:05:28,620 --> 01:05:30,822
(Please submit
the Code Deduction turn order.)

1492
01:05:31,390 --> 01:05:33,794
(Round Two: 1. Superman, 2. Ted,
3. Dark Knight)

1493
01:05:33,795 --> 01:05:36,229
(4. Gray, 5. Go Ae Shin,
6. Nangja, 7. Michael, 8. Banu)

1494
01:05:36,230 --> 01:05:38,363
(9. Benjamin, 10. Sugar,
11. Genie, 12. Hippo, 13. Polar Bear)

1495
01:05:38,664 --> 01:05:41,065
Round Two begins now.

1496
01:05:41,234 --> 01:05:43,368
Let's hold the line just like Round One.

1497
01:05:44,036 --> 01:05:46,137
Should we just cruise through Round Two...

1498
01:05:46,138 --> 01:05:47,772
and make our play in Round Three?

1499
01:05:50,776 --> 01:05:52,343
My favorite time,

1500
01:05:52,344 --> 01:05:54,812
nighttime, is creeping in.

1501
01:05:55,047 --> 01:05:57,482
I can't bring myself to trust anyone here.

1502
01:05:57,950 --> 01:05:59,617
Everything feels tainted by doubt.

1503
01:05:59,885 --> 01:06:01,786
I just want everyone to get along.

1504
01:06:02,154 --> 01:06:04,222
Option One, Dark Knight.

1505
01:06:04,657 --> 01:06:05,991
If I...

1506
01:06:06,692 --> 01:06:08,059
take Option Two...

1507
01:06:08,361 --> 01:06:10,228
I lock in my target, submit, and walk out.

1508
01:06:10,229 --> 01:06:11,797
They might be clocking us again.

1509
01:06:26,178 --> 01:06:27,211
Gray.

1510
01:06:29,081 --> 01:06:30,882
(Gray)

1511
01:06:34,020 --> 01:06:35,520
(Gray)

1512
01:06:36,355 --> 01:06:39,557
(All eyes turn to Gray.)

1513
01:06:39,558 --> 01:06:42,560
Can I say something in my defense?

1514
01:06:42,561 --> 01:06:45,730
A lot of the suspicion around me
feels purely vibe-based.

1515
01:06:46,065 --> 01:06:48,767
Earning trust while staying cautious.

1516
01:06:48,768 --> 01:06:50,201
That's more like a compliment.

1517
01:06:50,202 --> 01:06:53,338
- It is.
- Everyone in here plays that way.

1518
01:06:53,539 --> 01:06:56,841
There are no real hard clues out there.

1519
01:06:57,143 --> 01:06:59,911
So I don't get why multiple people...

1520
01:06:59,912 --> 01:07:03,181
are suddenly zeroing in on me.

1521
01:07:03,182 --> 01:07:06,685
Looking at the pieces I put together,

1522
01:07:07,186 --> 01:07:10,021
I found plenty of reasons
to doubt Ted as well.

1523
01:07:11,824 --> 01:07:14,226
Ask me whatever you want.

1524
01:07:14,227 --> 01:07:17,295
I'll lay it all out,
and I welcome the scrutiny.

1525
01:07:18,698 --> 01:07:19,765
Still...

1526
01:07:19,965 --> 01:07:21,265
people tend to assume the opposite...

1527
01:07:21,266 --> 01:07:24,001
of division is falling in line together.

1528
01:07:24,104 --> 01:07:27,205
Yet right now, we're forcing everyone
into the exact same mold.

1529
01:07:30,076 --> 01:07:32,044
We haven't left any room...

1530
01:07:32,511 --> 01:07:34,412
for different viewpoints.

1531
01:07:35,147 --> 01:07:36,914
- True.
- In the name of saving everyone,

1532
01:07:36,982 --> 01:07:39,116
we're setting up an overbearing system...

1533
01:07:39,117 --> 01:07:41,085
and piling on strict rules.

1534
01:07:41,086 --> 01:07:43,521
The harder we push for total alignment...

1535
01:07:43,522 --> 01:07:45,356
the more certain people...

1536
01:07:45,357 --> 01:07:47,058
might feel boxed in against their will.

1537
01:07:47,860 --> 01:07:49,561
That's a very real reaction.

1538
01:07:50,763 --> 01:07:54,199
What I'm saying is, forcing a consensus...

1539
01:07:54,734 --> 01:07:57,469
might look like perfect harmony
from the outside.

1540
01:07:57,703 --> 01:08:00,805
When we shut down opposing voices...

1541
01:08:00,806 --> 01:08:03,274
and demand universal compliance, though...

1542
01:08:03,275 --> 01:08:05,009
that in itself can be a form of division.

1543
01:08:05,010 --> 01:08:07,445
So you're saying that behavior alone
gives away the spy?

1544
01:08:07,980 --> 01:08:09,781
The person pushing for that...

1545
01:08:09,782 --> 01:08:11,549
- Pushing for it?
- and forcing everyone...

1546
01:08:11,550 --> 01:08:12,917
to think in lockstep...

1547
01:08:12,918 --> 01:08:14,353
is bound to make people uneasy.

1548
01:08:14,354 --> 01:08:16,355
And whoever drives that pressure...

1549
01:08:16,356 --> 01:08:17,855
could very well be the spy.

1550
01:08:18,090 --> 01:08:19,824
Which only makes me doubt Ted a bit more.

1551
01:08:19,825 --> 01:08:20,759
Hearing that, I can't help but...

1552
01:08:20,760 --> 01:08:23,061
Say what you want.
I know you're talking about me.

1553
01:08:23,062 --> 01:08:24,362
I assumed you were aiming that at me.

1554
01:08:24,530 --> 01:08:25,396
No, not you.

1555
01:08:25,397 --> 01:08:27,365
I mean, I'm the reason
we kept going down this road.

1556
01:08:27,366 --> 01:08:30,168
I stopped fixating
on obvious troublemakers...

1557
01:08:30,169 --> 01:08:33,438
and started watching the people
who build trust to stay untouchable.

1558
01:08:33,439 --> 01:08:35,074
I asked myself if one of them
could be the spy.

1559
01:08:35,075 --> 01:08:36,808
That's when my perspective shifted.

1560
01:08:36,976 --> 01:08:38,509
And that pointed straight to Ted.

1561
01:08:38,611 --> 01:08:41,112
It seems like everyone here...

1562
01:08:41,113 --> 01:08:43,548
puts blind trust in Ted.

1563
01:08:43,649 --> 01:08:45,083
And that's what makes him suspicious.

1564
01:08:46,051 --> 01:08:48,519
(Ted)

1565
01:08:49,522 --> 01:08:52,356
(Polar Bear wraps up the final turn
of Round Two.)

1566
01:08:53,025 --> 01:08:55,827
(Ideology Code Game: Round Two)

1567
01:08:55,828 --> 01:08:58,096
In my own defense,

1568
01:08:58,462 --> 01:09:00,632
I keep worrying
whether I'm constructing...

1569
01:09:00,633 --> 01:09:03,535
a system that stifles everyone
under mob rule.

1570
01:09:03,536 --> 01:09:05,670
I question myself constantly.

1571
01:09:06,272 --> 01:09:09,674
So please, bring up any doubt you have,
no matter how small.

1572
01:09:09,675 --> 01:09:11,243
There's one more thing...

1573
01:09:11,244 --> 01:09:13,011
that crossed my mind today.

1574
01:09:13,679 --> 01:09:16,748
We know the spy's mission is division.

1575
01:09:16,749 --> 01:09:18,751
- But we don't know the exact objective.
- Not at all.

1576
01:09:18,752 --> 01:09:19,917
I still genuinely...

1577
01:09:20,186 --> 01:09:22,254
believe paradise is within reach.

1578
01:09:22,555 --> 01:09:25,492
Maybe this entire setup was designed...

1579
01:09:25,493 --> 01:09:26,825
just to keep us on edge.

1580
01:09:27,793 --> 01:09:29,861
Maybe there's still
a one percent chance...

1581
01:09:29,862 --> 01:09:30,928
we all walk out of this alive.

1582
01:09:30,929 --> 01:09:31,796
Could be.

1583
01:09:32,097 --> 01:09:33,964
Living with a bad actor...

1584
01:09:33,965 --> 01:09:35,800
is just a reality of society.

1585
01:09:35,801 --> 01:09:37,101
Maybe that's what this represents.

1586
01:09:37,603 --> 01:09:39,438
Society never weeds out every bad apple.

1587
01:09:39,439 --> 01:09:41,072
There will always be outliers.

1588
01:09:41,407 --> 01:09:44,075
Maybe this whole thing is a trial.

1589
01:09:44,076 --> 01:09:46,577
- That's how I view it.
- To test who we turn into...

1590
01:09:46,578 --> 01:09:48,213
when the heat is on.

1591
01:09:48,347 --> 01:09:50,447
This could all just be fear
running the show.

1592
01:09:50,448 --> 01:09:52,884
That's why I'm not giving up
on the dream of paradise.

1593
01:09:52,885 --> 01:09:55,520
I can't bring myself to let it go.

1594
01:09:55,788 --> 01:09:57,822
If we're all willing to take this leap,

1595
01:09:58,491 --> 01:10:00,258
I want to bet...

1596
01:10:00,259 --> 01:10:01,394
on that one percent chance.

1597
01:10:01,395 --> 01:10:05,129
All 13 residents have
completed their checks.

1598
01:10:05,865 --> 01:10:09,167
During this second check phase,

1599
01:10:09,902 --> 01:10:13,304
one Ideology Check was attempted.

1600
01:10:17,443 --> 01:10:19,444
The number of successful checks is...

1601
01:10:25,217 --> 01:10:27,285
zero.

1602
01:10:27,820 --> 01:10:28,787
What does that tell us?

1603
01:10:28,921 --> 01:10:30,455
Does that mean the person attacking
wasn't the spy?

1604
01:10:30,456 --> 01:10:31,856
Go check your status...

1605
01:10:32,225 --> 01:10:34,926
at the Community Center.

1606
01:10:41,100 --> 01:10:42,333
Should we go in one at a time?

1607
01:10:42,334 --> 01:10:44,102
I'm going to check.

1608
01:10:44,103 --> 01:10:46,471
- But no one died.
- Not a single person.

1609
01:10:46,739 --> 01:10:48,006
Since no one died...

1610
01:10:48,007 --> 01:10:49,874
Let's think about this for a minute.

1611
01:10:49,875 --> 01:10:51,710
The spy can still attack someone...

1612
01:10:51,711 --> 01:10:53,578
while pretending to check on them.

1613
01:10:53,579 --> 01:10:55,315
They can start pulling tricks now.

1614
01:10:55,316 --> 01:10:57,449
They can rack up kills back-to-back.

1615
01:10:57,450 --> 01:10:59,084
- They can attack again?
- Exactly.

1616
01:10:59,485 --> 01:11:00,318
Until the round ends.

1617
01:11:00,319 --> 01:11:02,488
They can kill while pretending to check.

1618
01:11:04,056 --> 01:11:06,290
Even if time is running out,
there's plenty of time.

1619
01:11:06,291 --> 01:11:08,292
It takes seconds to eliminate someone.

1620
01:11:08,293 --> 01:11:09,727
They already have the codes.

1621
01:11:09,895 --> 01:11:11,829
Right. They can enter them all at once.

1622
01:11:11,830 --> 01:11:13,865
We have to go back in
for Round Three anyway.

1623
01:11:13,866 --> 01:11:15,734
If we're going to check, let's do it then.

1624
01:11:16,569 --> 01:11:20,205
But who in this room
turned on us like that?

1625
01:11:20,439 --> 01:11:22,206
I was honestly shocked.

1626
01:11:22,207 --> 01:11:23,809
Someone actually attacked.

1627
01:11:23,810 --> 01:11:25,077
Who was it?

1628
01:11:25,945 --> 01:11:26,912
Was it Michael?

1629
01:11:27,646 --> 01:11:28,923
Who tried to take someone out?

1630
01:11:28,948 --> 01:11:29,948
Grab the popcorn.

1631
01:11:30,249 --> 01:11:33,017
That's when I lost my temper a bit.

1632
01:11:33,018 --> 01:11:34,886
Enough of the nonsense.

1633
01:11:34,887 --> 01:11:37,188
This is getting real.

1634
01:11:37,189 --> 01:11:39,624
Several people could drop in Round Three.

1635
01:11:39,825 --> 01:11:41,692
This is the real deal.

1636
01:11:41,860 --> 01:11:44,261
We're dealing with an actual threat.

1637
01:11:44,630 --> 01:11:47,498
We're running out the clock
just playing along.

1638
01:11:47,499 --> 01:11:49,368
It's time to stop
with the wishful thinking.

1639
01:11:49,369 --> 01:11:52,737
- Fair point.
- We've spent six days talking about hope.

1640
01:11:52,738 --> 01:11:53,837
That's also true.

1641
01:11:53,838 --> 01:11:57,342
The moment we face reality,
we retreat right back to wishful thinking.

1642
01:11:57,343 --> 01:11:58,799
It was hard for me to bring up...

1643
01:11:58,823 --> 01:12:00,712
- something this uncomfortable.
- Got it.

1644
01:12:00,713 --> 01:12:03,681
We can't keep doing this.
We have 19 minutes left.

1645
01:12:04,216 --> 01:12:09,020
All this abstract talk
about the spy has just become...

1646
01:12:09,021 --> 01:12:11,722
an excuse to keep kicking
the can down the road.

1647
01:12:11,924 --> 01:12:13,891
Like ignoring overdue chores.

1648
01:12:13,892 --> 01:12:15,059
Like letting food waste sit.

1649
01:12:15,060 --> 01:12:17,295
We ignored it, and it just kept piling up.

1650
01:12:17,296 --> 01:12:19,131
Now the bag has burst.

1651
01:12:19,632 --> 01:12:23,501
And now we have to clean up the mess...

1652
01:12:23,502 --> 01:12:26,504
and handle this disaster immediately.

1653
01:12:26,905 --> 01:12:29,406
Round Two is already over.

1654
01:12:29,608 --> 01:12:31,342
Round Three is about to start.

1655
01:12:31,410 --> 01:12:34,245
Someone has already been attacked.

1656
01:12:34,246 --> 01:12:37,215
Was it the spy or someone else?

1657
01:12:37,216 --> 01:12:38,450
We have no idea.

1658
01:12:41,887 --> 01:12:44,223
So I'm proposing...

1659
01:12:44,224 --> 01:12:46,324
the only real way out I see.

1660
01:12:46,325 --> 01:12:47,391
The hard solution is...

1661
01:12:47,392 --> 01:12:51,429
to narrow down our suspects...

1662
01:12:51,764 --> 01:12:54,533
to one single target
based on our best read.

1663
01:12:54,900 --> 01:12:58,236
Then team up to neutralize them...

1664
01:12:58,237 --> 01:13:00,838
before they can attack anyone else.

1665
01:13:00,839 --> 01:13:02,507
Once the round is over,

1666
01:13:02,608 --> 01:13:04,375
we let them defend themselves.

1667
01:13:04,376 --> 01:13:06,278
Then we decide whether to revive them.

1668
01:13:06,578 --> 01:13:08,078
That makes sense.

1669
01:13:08,079 --> 01:13:09,313
Sounds solid.

1670
01:13:09,415 --> 01:13:11,449
- Focus on the prime suspect.
- Right.

1671
01:13:11,450 --> 01:13:12,951
That way, we still have a chance
to bring them back.

1672
01:13:12,952 --> 01:13:15,453
We can hear their side of the story...

1673
01:13:15,454 --> 01:13:17,922
and decide together.

1674
01:13:18,090 --> 01:13:19,157
- Sounds like a plan.
- Agreed.

1675
01:13:19,158 --> 01:13:20,491
I'm in too.

1676
01:13:20,793 --> 01:13:22,693
Let's take a vote first.

1677
01:13:22,694 --> 01:13:24,395
Let's talk it through one more time.

1678
01:13:24,396 --> 01:13:26,031
Call out your suspect.

1679
01:13:26,032 --> 01:13:27,899
Speak up, please.

1680
01:13:27,900 --> 01:13:30,468
Write down the names brought up earlier.

1681
01:13:30,469 --> 01:13:31,903
First, Dark Knight.

1682
01:13:31,904 --> 01:13:33,004
Second, Ted.

1683
01:13:33,172 --> 01:13:34,205
Third, Gray.

1684
01:13:35,107 --> 01:13:37,175
(The suspects put forward
their own names.)

1685
01:13:37,502 --> 01:13:39,279
I still think we should
keep an eye on Nangja.

1686
01:13:39,311 --> 01:13:40,245
Nangja, got it.

1687
01:13:40,246 --> 01:13:43,080
I like her, but her role is suspicious.

1688
01:13:43,615 --> 01:13:45,115
That matters too.

1689
01:13:45,116 --> 01:13:49,563
Rebuilding trust with the Reporter...

1690
01:13:49,588 --> 01:13:50,888
is just as crucial.

1691
01:13:53,759 --> 01:13:55,426
Let's take this to the situation room.

1692
01:13:55,427 --> 01:13:58,963
I'll open the chat room.

1693
01:13:59,431 --> 01:14:01,598
Drop in and tell me...

1694
01:14:01,599 --> 01:14:04,535
- who you picked.
- Okay.

1695
01:14:04,803 --> 01:14:05,936
Let me know.

1696
01:14:08,574 --> 01:14:09,641
Are you in?

1697
01:14:09,642 --> 01:14:13,745
First, Hippo. Second, Benjamin.

1698
01:14:14,046 --> 01:14:14,911
Got it.

1699
01:14:16,148 --> 01:14:17,482
This feels...

1700
01:14:18,518 --> 01:14:21,085
I worry this is just a quick fix.

1701
01:14:21,086 --> 01:14:23,555
We're flying completely blind.

1702
01:14:23,556 --> 01:14:24,722
Exactly my point.

1703
01:14:24,723 --> 01:14:25,790
Zero clues.

1704
01:14:25,791 --> 01:14:28,092
We're presuming those four are guilty.

1705
01:14:28,393 --> 01:14:30,995
- Even so...
- Done.

1706
01:14:31,463 --> 01:14:33,531
We're under the gun here.

1707
01:14:33,866 --> 01:14:34,833
I can handle it.

1708
01:14:35,901 --> 01:14:38,202
I get why I look suspicious.

1709
01:14:38,203 --> 01:14:40,005
Just because a name gets tossed around,

1710
01:14:40,238 --> 01:14:42,273
that makes them a target for elimination?

1711
01:14:43,041 --> 01:14:45,275
Benjamin and Superman.

1712
01:14:46,979 --> 01:14:48,178
Gray and...

1713
01:14:48,647 --> 01:14:50,281
Dark Knight.

1714
01:14:51,083 --> 01:14:52,919
Those two were singled out...

1715
01:14:52,920 --> 01:14:54,552
purely on gut feelings.

1716
01:14:54,553 --> 01:14:56,822
You're basically saying,
"Take the blame now. Fix it later."

1717
01:14:58,957 --> 01:14:59,547
Right.

1718
01:14:59,571 --> 01:15:02,893
This is going to turn into a witch hunt.

1719
01:15:05,030 --> 01:15:07,798
It already is one.

1720
01:15:07,966 --> 01:15:08,967
What is this, then?

1721
01:15:09,868 --> 01:15:11,503
It's a kangaroo court.

1722
01:15:13,005 --> 01:15:14,839
I checked Dark Knight.

1723
01:15:15,408 --> 01:15:17,875
Then I checked Gray in Round Two.

1724
01:15:19,378 --> 01:15:22,080
Hold on. Everyone, stay where you are.

1725
01:15:22,081 --> 01:15:25,917
I'd like to make a formal objection.

1726
01:15:25,918 --> 01:15:26,784
Go ahead.

1727
01:15:27,354 --> 01:15:30,154
No one goes back in during Round Two.

1728
01:15:30,155 --> 01:15:31,389
You're going in Round Three?

1729
01:15:31,590 --> 01:15:33,457
- Yeah.
- Then hold on a second.

1730
01:15:33,458 --> 01:15:35,627
I'm putting the brakes on this right now.

1731
01:15:42,434 --> 01:15:44,734
Step outside for a second.
We need to pause.

1732
01:15:44,735 --> 01:15:45,770
I have something to say.

1733
01:15:45,771 --> 01:15:46,604
All right.

1734
01:15:49,174 --> 01:15:50,875
Listen up, everyone. Is everyone here?

1735
01:15:50,876 --> 01:15:52,810
Who was the one person earlier?

1736
01:15:53,145 --> 01:15:54,245
Okay.

1737
01:15:54,847 --> 01:15:57,282
I don't know who the spy is...

1738
01:15:57,283 --> 01:15:58,983
because I don't have the facts.

1739
01:16:00,085 --> 01:16:01,118
But that's beside the point.

1740
01:16:01,119 --> 01:16:03,587
I'm against picking four people...

1741
01:16:03,588 --> 01:16:04,990
just to single out a primary suspect.

1742
01:16:05,257 --> 01:16:07,758
Targeting whoever gets mentioned most...

1743
01:16:07,759 --> 01:16:10,261
turns this whole thing into a witch hunt.

1744
01:16:10,262 --> 01:16:11,396
Look at what happened before.

1745
01:16:12,030 --> 01:16:14,232
Michael was suspected right off the bat...

1746
01:16:14,233 --> 01:16:16,266
just because he talked
about the spy a lot.

1747
01:16:16,267 --> 01:16:17,868
- But he was clean.
- Exactly.

1748
01:16:17,869 --> 01:16:20,704
And especially with these two,

1749
01:16:20,705 --> 01:16:23,874
Gray was running around
warning everyone...

1750
01:16:23,875 --> 01:16:25,209
about what the spy might do.

1751
01:16:25,644 --> 01:16:28,979
Ted was doing everything he could
to stop the spy too.

1752
01:16:28,980 --> 01:16:32,283
For four straight days, we kept the peace.

1753
01:16:32,484 --> 01:16:34,451
Now the two people
trying to stop the spy...

1754
01:16:34,452 --> 01:16:36,587
are being framed as the spy.

1755
01:16:36,588 --> 01:16:38,889
Look, what I mean is...

1756
01:16:38,890 --> 01:16:40,824
- No, let me finish.
- Go on.

1757
01:16:40,825 --> 01:16:44,271
You can't just slap
a guilty label on someone...

1758
01:16:44,296 --> 01:16:45,896
based on a random hunch.

1759
01:16:46,097 --> 01:16:47,731
Then offer a better solution.

1760
01:16:47,732 --> 01:16:50,267
That's what we need to figure out.

1761
01:16:50,268 --> 01:16:52,579
Are we seriously going
with "die first, ask questions later"?

1762
01:16:52,604 --> 01:16:55,005
We have nothing to go on right now.

1763
01:16:55,507 --> 01:16:57,341
- Look at it this way.
- Okay.

1764
01:16:57,342 --> 01:16:59,310
If we let things play out...

1765
01:16:59,311 --> 01:17:00,911
and someone drops dead,

1766
01:17:00,912 --> 01:17:01,879
is that fair?

1767
01:17:01,880 --> 01:17:03,648
Or is it better to pick one person,

1768
01:17:03,673 --> 01:17:05,382
take them out, and see what happens?

1769
01:17:05,684 --> 01:17:08,452
Neither option is fair.

1770
01:17:08,687 --> 01:17:09,721
- How so?
- But still...

1771
01:17:09,722 --> 01:17:11,489
This is completely unfair.

1772
01:17:11,490 --> 01:17:12,556
I'll admit that.

1773
01:17:12,791 --> 01:17:14,125
It isn't fair.

1774
01:17:14,126 --> 01:17:17,128
But this is just pooling
everyone's suspicions...

1775
01:17:17,129 --> 01:17:19,497
- like a straw poll.
- I disagree.

1776
01:17:19,498 --> 01:17:20,598
Don't speak for everyone.

1777
01:17:20,599 --> 01:17:22,066
I don't suspect these people at all.

1778
01:17:22,334 --> 01:17:23,868
Then who do you suspect?

1779
01:17:23,869 --> 01:17:24,869
I don't suspect anyone.

1780
01:17:25,036 --> 01:17:26,370
That's why I kept my mouth shut.

1781
01:17:26,371 --> 01:17:28,339
Honestly, then...

1782
01:17:28,340 --> 01:17:29,673
If someone comes after me...

1783
01:17:29,674 --> 01:17:31,141
and I get eliminated, that's the game.

1784
01:17:31,142 --> 01:17:33,978
- I don't get you.
- That's just how the game works.

1785
01:17:33,979 --> 01:17:36,480
What I don't get is...

1786
01:17:36,848 --> 01:17:39,717
Superman, why didn't you speak up before?

1787
01:17:39,718 --> 01:17:41,086
Because I don't know anything for certain.

1788
01:17:41,653 --> 01:17:43,287
You could still weigh in.

1789
01:17:43,288 --> 01:17:46,290
You think any of us know for sure?

1790
01:17:46,758 --> 01:17:50,227
None of us do. We're all guessing
at 20 or 30 percent confidence.

1791
01:17:50,395 --> 01:17:53,431
But if we never talk it through,

1792
01:17:53,432 --> 01:17:54,799
we'll get nowhere.

1793
01:17:54,800 --> 01:17:57,000
Put yourself in their shoes.

1794
01:17:57,202 --> 01:17:59,503
Say I kept pointing fingers at Genie...

1795
01:17:59,504 --> 01:18:01,606
and put a target on her back.

1796
01:18:01,607 --> 01:18:02,941
Would you sit back and say nothing?

1797
01:18:03,408 --> 01:18:04,675
- No.
- Of course not.

1798
01:18:05,477 --> 01:18:06,643
What about Ae Shin?

1799
01:18:06,644 --> 01:18:07,812
- She wouldn't take that sitting down.
- Not a chance.

1800
01:18:07,813 --> 01:18:09,581
- Same goes for Benjamin.
- I'd push back.

1801
01:18:09,981 --> 01:18:12,684
Tomorrow it could be me...

1802
01:18:12,685 --> 01:18:14,552
getting thrown under the bus.

1803
01:18:14,553 --> 01:18:17,355
Are we supposed to say, "Four names
came up. At least it wasn't me"...

1804
01:18:17,356 --> 01:18:18,757
and just shrug it off?

1805
01:18:18,758 --> 01:18:19,991
I don't know.

1806
01:18:20,359 --> 01:18:21,526
Then what's the move?

1807
01:18:21,527 --> 01:18:23,928
Yesterday, I told Michael...

1808
01:18:24,162 --> 01:18:27,431
that a brave dissenter saved the group.

1809
01:18:27,432 --> 01:18:29,534
So why can't you see where I'm standing...

1810
01:18:30,903 --> 01:18:32,469
as speaking up when it matters?

1811
01:18:32,838 --> 01:18:35,106
Superman throwing in this one objection...

1812
01:18:35,107 --> 01:18:36,974
has ground everything to a halt.

1813
01:18:36,975 --> 01:18:38,142
We're completely paralyzed.

1814
01:18:38,143 --> 01:18:40,178
- We sat on our hands for six days.
- That's not the point.

1815
01:18:40,179 --> 01:18:41,679
Don't take Michael's panic...

1816
01:18:41,680 --> 01:18:43,648
- I'm not panicking.
- and project it onto the room.

1817
01:18:43,815 --> 01:18:45,582
What about these four people, then?

1818
01:18:45,583 --> 01:18:46,518
Because you're scared,

1819
01:18:46,543 --> 01:18:48,886
you're sending them
straight to the chopping block.

1820
01:18:48,887 --> 01:18:50,254
- We can't do this.
- It's not my fear.

1821
01:18:50,255 --> 01:18:53,156
Didn't you say someone
had to say the hard truth?

1822
01:18:53,157 --> 01:18:55,225
I'm saying it right now.

1823
01:18:56,896 --> 01:18:58,362
The way I see it...

1824
01:18:59,798 --> 01:19:01,031
right now,

1825
01:19:02,434 --> 01:19:05,203
I see why Superman only pulled two votes.

1826
01:19:10,209 --> 01:19:11,508
We put them on the spot, sure.

1827
01:19:11,509 --> 01:19:13,277
But that was completely uncalled for.

1828
01:19:13,278 --> 01:19:15,479
Keep personal attacks out of this.

1829
01:19:15,480 --> 01:19:17,681
Don't cross that line.
Leave that out of this.

1830
01:19:17,682 --> 01:19:20,885
I respect Superman, of course.

1831
01:19:20,886 --> 01:19:22,486
I'm not being emotional here.

1832
01:19:22,487 --> 01:19:24,188
The contradiction is...

1833
01:19:24,189 --> 01:19:27,558
the leader already made the call.

1834
01:19:27,559 --> 01:19:30,227
And the second we try to move forward,

1835
01:19:30,996 --> 01:19:31,796
you derail the whole thing?

1836
01:19:31,797 --> 01:19:33,698
I think you're entitled to speak up.

1837
01:19:38,537 --> 01:19:41,639
If an elimination is unavoidable,

1838
01:19:41,840 --> 01:19:44,675
Michael's approach was far more pragmatic.

1839
01:19:44,676 --> 01:19:46,911
There was no reason to scrap it.

1840
01:19:46,912 --> 01:19:49,146
I side with Superman on this.

1841
01:19:49,147 --> 01:19:51,515
It's basic due process.

1842
01:19:51,650 --> 01:19:54,518
People used to be purged like that.

1843
01:19:54,686 --> 01:19:55,954
We can't go down that road.

1844
01:19:56,254 --> 01:19:57,955
I want to ask the leader...

1845
01:19:57,956 --> 01:19:59,825
if this genuinely honors due process...

1846
01:19:59,850 --> 01:20:01,549
the way you insisted it should.

1847
01:20:01,893 --> 01:20:03,961
We need an answer
that clearly addresses that.

1848
01:20:03,962 --> 01:20:06,597
The second round is over.

1849
01:20:08,600 --> 01:20:10,968
The third round begins now.

1850
01:20:12,838 --> 01:20:16,040
Leader, please report
to the Center within five minutes...

1851
01:20:16,341 --> 01:20:18,409
to set the running order.

1852
01:20:21,646 --> 01:20:23,146
Wait. Let me say something.

1853
01:20:23,147 --> 01:20:25,148
I get what Superman is saying.

1854
01:20:25,149 --> 01:20:26,950
The system is broken.

1855
01:20:26,951 --> 01:20:27,818
Right.

1856
01:20:27,819 --> 01:20:31,655
But right now we have a revival token.

1857
01:20:31,656 --> 01:20:36,159
So let's target a prime suspect first,
just this once...

1858
01:20:36,160 --> 01:20:38,195
and fix the system afterward.

1859
01:20:38,196 --> 01:20:40,430
We only have four minutes
and forty seconds.

1860
01:20:40,431 --> 01:20:42,799
Go lock in the order and come back.

1861
01:20:42,800 --> 01:20:44,368
We can keep talking while you're gone.

1862
01:20:44,369 --> 01:20:46,937
But the vote isn't even finished.

1863
01:20:47,906 --> 01:20:48,773
- Not yet.
- Exactly.

1864
01:20:48,774 --> 01:20:51,542
We need to act fast.

1865
01:20:51,543 --> 01:20:52,510
Leave the call to the leader.

1866
01:20:52,511 --> 01:20:55,813
I'll decide the Round Three order myself.

1867
01:20:56,414 --> 01:20:59,916
As long as anyone has doubts
about this process,

1868
01:21:00,084 --> 01:21:02,753
we can't pretend everyone agreed to it.

1869
01:21:02,754 --> 01:21:04,287
The process I proposed...

1870
01:21:04,789 --> 01:21:07,925
was to rank the suspects...

1871
01:21:08,093 --> 01:21:09,828
and select a target.

1872
01:21:09,829 --> 01:21:11,796
We never reached consensus on that.

1873
01:21:11,797 --> 01:21:16,199
So standing down
from a coordinated attack...

1874
01:21:16,200 --> 01:21:19,369
is what minimizes harm to the group.

1875
01:21:20,405 --> 01:21:23,841
(Polar Bear backs Superman's stance.)

1876
01:21:25,710 --> 01:21:27,611
In the end, he got his way.

1877
01:21:27,812 --> 01:21:29,748
All he did was put...

1878
01:21:29,773 --> 01:21:33,183
the worst traits of politicians
on display.

1879
01:21:33,454 --> 01:21:36,720
He offered zero solutions,
just sat there arguing with me.

1880
01:21:37,022 --> 01:21:39,623
It looked like pure performance.

1881
01:21:40,091 --> 01:21:42,993
I'm sorry, but real stakes
are on the line.

1882
01:21:43,195 --> 01:21:46,097
This isn't a TV debate anymore.

1883
01:21:48,466 --> 01:21:53,703
(Round Three order locked in)

1884
01:21:55,874 --> 01:21:57,478
(R3: Go Ae Shin, Michael, Banu, Benjamin)

1885
01:21:57,479 --> 01:21:59,215
(Sugar, Genie, Superman,
Polar Bear, Hippo)

1886
01:21:59,216 --> 01:22:00,811
(Gray, Nangja, Dark Knight, Ted)

1887
01:22:01,513 --> 01:22:03,914
Round Three begins now.

1888
01:22:08,386 --> 01:22:09,286
(Select an action.)

1889
01:22:09,287 --> 01:22:10,487
(1. View score, 2. Attack,
3. Transfer immunity card)

1890
01:22:17,462 --> 01:22:20,330
I'm picking Superman this round.

1891
01:22:27,005 --> 01:22:30,274
Several people have already gone through.

1892
01:22:30,275 --> 01:22:33,076
- Single-target focus is off the table.
- Obviously.

1893
01:22:33,077 --> 01:22:35,679
Tensions are running high,

1894
01:22:35,948 --> 01:22:37,948
but let's not lose our heads.

1895
01:22:37,949 --> 01:22:39,817
I want to apologize again.

1896
01:22:40,184 --> 01:22:41,518
For the low blow earlier.

1897
01:22:41,519 --> 01:22:43,787
You don't need to apologize for that.

1898
01:22:44,265 --> 01:22:46,967
If you normalize this behavior,
when you're on the chopping block,

1899
01:22:46,992 --> 01:22:48,460
nobody will stick their neck out for you.

1900
01:22:49,394 --> 01:22:51,528
- What does that supposed to mean?
- Look...

1901
01:22:51,529 --> 01:22:52,696
- I'm saying...
- Guys, stop.

1902
01:22:52,697 --> 01:22:54,798
- Drop it.
- If no one speaks out now,

1903
01:22:55,132 --> 01:22:58,268
when your time comes,
no one will speak up for you.

1904
01:22:58,403 --> 01:22:59,904
That's why I'm raising this.

1905
01:23:00,005 --> 01:23:02,039
There's barely five minutes left.

1906
01:23:02,040 --> 01:23:04,075
Wait, look at the bigger picture here.

1907
01:23:04,076 --> 01:23:06,777
If no one gets eliminated again,

1908
01:23:06,778 --> 01:23:08,246
it might feel like a relief,

1909
01:23:08,247 --> 01:23:11,315
- We're stuck playing another game.
- but kicking the problem down the line...

1910
01:23:11,950 --> 01:23:15,252
could mean an even steeper
body count later.

1911
01:23:15,253 --> 01:23:16,487
It could be far more brutal.

1912
01:23:16,488 --> 01:23:18,789
The fallout could hit us twice as hard.

1913
01:23:18,790 --> 01:23:21,825
Let's just put this argument to rest.

1914
01:23:21,826 --> 01:23:23,427
I'll drop it too.

1915
01:23:23,428 --> 01:23:26,297
Everyone's backed into a corner right now.

1916
01:23:26,298 --> 01:23:28,232
Second-guessing everything will only...

1917
01:23:28,233 --> 01:23:31,501
Resident Gray,

1918
01:23:31,502 --> 01:23:34,771
please report to the Community Center now.

1919
01:23:34,772 --> 01:23:36,206
I feel the same way.

1920
01:23:36,207 --> 01:23:37,308
For one thing, I...

1921
01:23:37,876 --> 01:23:38,909
was singled out as a suspect.

1922
01:23:38,910 --> 01:23:40,544
So I had to keep my mouth shut.

1923
01:23:40,612 --> 01:23:43,247
Still, this whole mess...

1924
01:23:43,248 --> 01:23:44,748
shows who we really are.

1925
01:23:44,749 --> 01:23:46,317
We all made our choices.

1926
01:23:46,584 --> 01:23:49,620
Some pushed hard.

1927
01:23:49,621 --> 01:23:52,022
Some pushed back, and some stayed quiet.

1928
01:23:52,090 --> 01:23:55,759
Every single one of us
brought about this outcome.

1929
01:23:55,760 --> 01:23:57,561
It's too late to unwind it now.

1930
01:23:57,562 --> 01:23:59,763
Let's see the results...

1931
01:24:00,264 --> 01:24:01,464
- and regroup from there.
- Fair enough.

1932
01:24:01,465 --> 01:24:04,367
- Let's all cool off until then.
- Right.

1933
01:24:04,903 --> 01:24:06,704
Things are only going downhill from here.

1934
01:24:07,438 --> 01:24:09,606
Our defense is completely cracked.

1935
01:24:09,909 --> 01:24:12,843
We held on to this ideal.

1936
01:24:12,944 --> 01:24:16,446
Now it's looking like a failed experiment.

1937
01:24:16,715 --> 01:24:18,449
This place is already miserable.

1938
01:24:18,450 --> 01:24:20,785
Where is this supposed paradise?

1939
01:24:21,019 --> 01:24:22,152
It's pure delusion.

1940
01:24:22,253 --> 01:24:24,521
There is no setup...

1941
01:24:24,522 --> 01:24:26,590
where everyone walks away happy.

1942
01:24:27,392 --> 01:24:31,061
Did someone pull another ideology check?

1943
01:24:32,263 --> 01:24:33,797
I bet they did.

1944
01:24:34,366 --> 01:24:36,100
Anyone, spy or not,

1945
01:24:36,101 --> 01:24:38,369
could get greedy.

1946
01:24:38,870 --> 01:24:40,737
This chaos is the perfect cover.

1947
01:24:40,738 --> 01:24:42,538
- It's prime time for a big payday.
- Exactly.

1948
01:24:42,539 --> 01:24:43,707
Right.

1949
01:24:44,518 --> 01:24:45,652
(Select an action.)

1950
01:24:45,677 --> 01:24:47,779
Would you like to run an ideology check?

1951
01:25:05,964 --> 01:25:08,866
(Benjamin matches scores with Banu.)

1952
01:25:09,134 --> 01:25:10,102
I'll run Banu.

1953
01:25:10,103 --> 01:25:11,102
Ideology check.

1954
01:25:11,103 --> 01:25:11,769
(Score: 8)

1955
01:25:13,037 --> 01:25:14,871
(Right 1, Equalism 1,
Upper-middle 2, Conservative 1)

1956
01:25:15,907 --> 01:25:18,409
(Michael)

1957
01:25:19,511 --> 01:25:21,679
(Benjamin runs an attack on Michael.)

1958
01:25:22,213 --> 01:25:23,515
Michael has been eliminated.

1959
01:25:24,916 --> 01:25:26,016
Success.

1960
01:25:26,552 --> 01:25:28,752
Your ideology check matched.

1961
01:25:28,753 --> 01:25:30,687
(Michael's funds will be
transferred to you.)

1962
01:25:30,688 --> 01:25:33,024
One, he keeps forcing me into English.

1963
01:25:33,025 --> 01:25:34,858
I want him out sooner rather than later.

1964
01:25:34,859 --> 01:25:37,594
Two, he constantly stirs up trouble.

1965
01:25:37,595 --> 01:25:39,630
You don't do that to your own team.

1966
01:25:39,631 --> 01:25:41,865
At some point, a line has to be drawn.

1967
01:25:41,866 --> 01:25:42,899
You can't let that slide.

1968
01:25:43,001 --> 01:25:48,205
He pushed for an action
that completely lacked legitimacy.

1969
01:25:48,506 --> 01:25:50,708
I wanted to balance the scales.

1970
01:25:50,709 --> 01:25:52,619
In the name of the greater good,
even coming from the spy,

1971
01:25:52,644 --> 01:25:54,445
farewell, Michael.

1972
01:25:58,183 --> 01:26:01,852
All 13 residents have finished
checking scores.

1973
01:26:01,853 --> 01:26:03,354
(Ideology Code Game: Round Three)

1974
01:26:03,455 --> 01:26:06,357
During the third round,

1975
01:26:06,558 --> 01:26:09,994
two ideology attacks were launched.

1976
01:26:12,030 --> 01:26:13,797
The number of successful checks is...

1977
01:26:18,937 --> 01:26:22,006
two.

1978
01:26:23,775 --> 01:26:29,179
There are now two casualties.

1979
01:26:29,180 --> 01:26:30,080
Two people?

1980
01:26:32,417 --> 01:26:33,952
I was caught completely off guard.

1981
01:26:34,219 --> 01:26:37,988
I figured someone might go today.

1982
01:26:37,989 --> 01:26:40,357
I didn't expect two hits at once.

1983
01:26:40,358 --> 01:26:43,760
I took out one person,
so who hit the second?

1984
01:26:43,761 --> 01:26:46,463
Who did it? Who went rogue?

1985
01:26:47,532 --> 01:26:48,900
This just got interesting.

1986
01:26:50,368 --> 01:26:51,568
Check your status...

1987
01:26:51,870 --> 01:26:54,338
at the Community Center.

1988
01:26:54,506 --> 01:26:56,640
Let's go check our status first.

1989
01:26:56,708 --> 01:26:59,176
Residents who want to pass immunity...

1990
01:26:59,177 --> 01:27:03,881
must report to the Community Center
before time expires.

1991
01:27:07,118 --> 01:27:08,953
I'm here to see if I was attacked.

1992
01:27:10,289 --> 01:27:12,056
You were not attacked.

1993
01:27:16,127 --> 01:27:18,061
I want to know if I'm alive or out.

1994
01:27:18,730 --> 01:27:20,464
You were not attacked.

1995
01:27:22,734 --> 01:27:23,967
I'm clear.

1996
01:27:27,839 --> 01:27:29,373
Did Hippo make it?

1997
01:27:34,412 --> 01:27:35,445
You've been eliminated.

1998
01:27:37,448 --> 01:27:38,348
I'm in shock.

1999
01:27:39,617 --> 01:27:42,552
(Round Two)

2000
01:27:42,954 --> 01:27:44,922
Combined score check.

2001
01:27:45,123 --> 01:27:47,791
(Gray and Hippo's
combined score: 13 points)

2002
01:27:53,765 --> 01:27:56,667
(Day Two: the debate over Michael's vote)

2003
01:27:57,035 --> 01:27:58,120
Are you the spy?

2004
01:27:58,736 --> 01:28:00,737
No, I'm not the spy.

2005
01:28:00,738 --> 01:28:03,907
Gray was actually my top suspect.

2006
01:28:04,576 --> 01:28:07,077
She kept pointing the finger at me.

2007
01:28:07,078 --> 01:28:11,348
So I wondered
if Hippo was the real operative.

2008
01:28:11,349 --> 01:28:15,019
That's why I went after Hippo first.

2009
01:28:15,353 --> 01:28:17,588
Should we take the easy path?

2010
01:28:17,589 --> 01:28:19,489
Let's weed Hippo out first.

2011
01:28:19,791 --> 01:28:21,458
Hippo's the one I can pinpoint.

2012
01:28:26,264 --> 01:28:27,899
I'll run an ideology check.

2013
01:28:30,635 --> 01:28:31,502
(Hippo)

2014
01:28:31,503 --> 01:28:33,470
(Gray attempts a check on Hippo.)

2015
01:28:33,471 --> 01:28:35,672
(Left 3, Feminism 3,
Upper-middle 2, Open-minded 3)

2016
01:28:35,974 --> 01:28:38,242
Your ideology check failed.

2017
01:28:39,844 --> 01:28:42,546
(No penalty for a failed check)

2018
01:28:43,514 --> 01:28:45,815
(Round Three)

2019
01:28:46,384 --> 01:28:48,118
I'll launch an ideology attack.

2020
01:28:48,119 --> 01:28:50,487
(Additional attack token purchased)

2021
01:28:50,488 --> 01:28:51,320
(Hippo)

2022
01:28:51,321 --> 01:28:52,756
Looking at the numbers,

2023
01:28:52,991 --> 01:28:55,125
she was the highest-probability target.

2024
01:28:55,126 --> 01:28:57,695
I knew two tries would do it.

2025
01:28:58,228 --> 01:28:59,129
Success.

2026
01:29:00,431 --> 01:29:02,699
Your ideology check matched.

2027
01:29:03,167 --> 01:29:05,468
(Gray successfully checks Hippo.)

2028
01:29:05,469 --> 01:29:08,238
All of Hippo's personal funds
will be transferred to you.

2029
01:29:08,239 --> 01:29:09,806
(13,040 dollars, 0 dollars)

2030
01:29:15,346 --> 01:29:18,081
(Gray heads over to verify her survival.)

2031
01:29:19,117 --> 01:29:20,350
They told me I was hit.

2032
01:29:20,718 --> 01:29:22,452
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

2033
01:29:22,453 --> 01:29:23,219
Two casualties.

2034
01:29:23,788 --> 01:29:24,856
What happened, Hippo?

2035
01:29:25,089 --> 01:29:26,022
I got hit.

2036
01:29:29,327 --> 01:29:30,360
- For real?
- Yeah.

2037
01:29:32,531 --> 01:29:34,131
Guys, I'm out.

2038
01:29:34,132 --> 01:29:35,632
- What?
- I'm done.

2039
01:29:35,900 --> 01:29:37,201
Someone targeted me.

2040
01:29:38,169 --> 01:29:39,746
I was caught off guard for a second.

2041
01:29:39,771 --> 01:29:41,238
But we had an agreement...

2042
01:29:41,239 --> 01:29:44,951
to pool and share our immunity tokens.

2043
01:29:44,976 --> 01:29:46,276
So I wasn't really sweating it.

2044
01:29:46,678 --> 01:29:48,846
Everything happened just as predicted.

2045
01:29:50,057 --> 01:29:51,388
Like any game of Mafia,

2046
01:29:51,413 --> 01:29:53,150
someone has to take a hit
for the collective to gain information.

2047
01:29:53,151 --> 01:29:56,086
Two attacks, two hits.

2048
01:29:56,087 --> 01:29:57,154
I'm out.

2049
01:29:57,889 --> 01:29:59,422
I took the hit.

2050
01:30:01,693 --> 01:30:03,193
- You're serious?
- Dead serious.

2051
01:30:03,194 --> 01:30:04,228
Wait, guys.

2052
01:30:04,664 --> 01:30:06,730
Find the other casualty first,
so everyone else doesn't waste a trip.

2053
01:30:06,731 --> 01:30:07,598
You're out?

2054
01:30:07,599 --> 01:30:10,200
They went for high-percentage targets.

2055
01:30:10,201 --> 01:30:13,337
Whoever attacked earlier...

2056
01:30:13,771 --> 01:30:15,472
probably took another shot at me.

2057
01:30:16,141 --> 01:30:17,241
What did the screen say?

2058
01:30:17,308 --> 01:30:18,476
"You've been eliminated."

2059
01:30:22,947 --> 01:30:25,048
We have immunity tokens.

2060
01:30:25,917 --> 01:30:28,185
Who has one? She doesn't.

2061
01:30:28,386 --> 01:30:29,353
Transfer it over.

2062
01:30:34,792 --> 01:30:36,993
Honestly, I didn't see this coming.

2063
01:30:36,994 --> 01:30:39,796
I figured the rest of the room...

2064
01:30:39,797 --> 01:30:41,898
would take shots during Round Three.

2065
01:30:41,899 --> 01:30:44,134
I was thrown when nobody moved.

2066
01:30:44,135 --> 01:30:45,368
What a bunch of hypocrites.

2067
01:30:45,770 --> 01:30:47,237
They make a huge scene...

2068
01:30:47,472 --> 01:30:50,073
putting Gray on trial...

2069
01:30:50,074 --> 01:30:52,242
demanding we take down the spy,
and then chicken out?

2070
01:30:52,243 --> 01:30:53,677
It's ridiculous.

2071
01:30:53,911 --> 01:30:55,546
- Did I make it?
- Was I targeted?

2072
01:30:55,547 --> 01:30:57,781
- Am I safe?
- Check if anyone hit me.

2073
01:30:57,782 --> 01:30:58,815
Was I attacked?

2074
01:30:58,816 --> 01:30:59,716
Checking my status.

2075
01:30:59,717 --> 01:31:02,085
- Checking for hits.
- Seeing if I'm still in.

2076
01:31:02,820 --> 01:31:04,554
You were not attacked.

2077
01:31:05,590 --> 01:31:06,457
Thank you.

2078
01:31:08,059 --> 01:31:09,292
Well,

2079
01:31:10,461 --> 01:31:13,263
tell me if I took a hit.

2080
01:31:15,099 --> 01:31:16,199
You've been eliminated.

2081
01:31:16,701 --> 01:31:17,567
Understood.

2082
01:31:20,471 --> 01:31:21,738
I saw it coming.

2083
01:31:21,739 --> 01:31:24,207
Ever since Day Two,

2084
01:31:24,208 --> 01:31:27,577
I've been painted
as obsessing over the spy.

2085
01:31:27,578 --> 01:31:30,246
I'm used to the crosshairs being on me.

2086
01:31:30,414 --> 01:31:33,883
I figured Round Three would be my turn.

2087
01:31:34,152 --> 01:31:35,252
Sure enough.

2088
01:31:36,287 --> 01:31:37,487
Did someone else drop?

2089
01:31:37,488 --> 01:31:38,288
Michael.

2090
01:31:39,157 --> 01:31:40,591
- Michael's out?
- Yeah.

2091
01:31:41,526 --> 01:31:43,026
They singled out the two of us.

2092
01:31:43,027 --> 01:31:44,394
We're the two casualties.

2093
01:31:44,395 --> 01:31:46,730
Did the spy strike twice?

2094
01:31:46,731 --> 01:31:47,731
- Yeah.
- Exactly.

2095
01:31:48,699 --> 01:31:51,467
One attack in Round Two.

2096
01:31:53,771 --> 01:31:54,604
And...

2097
01:31:55,439 --> 01:31:58,441
two attacks in Round Three.

2098
01:31:58,442 --> 01:32:00,578
Did the spy burn all those tokens?

2099
01:32:00,945 --> 01:32:03,113
Then that wasn't the spy
pulling the trigger.

2100
01:32:03,881 --> 01:32:05,782
A third person might have done it.

2101
01:32:06,017 --> 01:32:09,253
Sorry, but we should discuss this later.

2102
01:32:09,278 --> 01:32:12,289
We promised to save them.

2103
01:32:12,290 --> 01:32:15,092
- Let's hear from those three.
- Let's hear what they think.

2104
01:32:15,226 --> 01:32:16,827
- Right.
- Quickly.

2105
01:32:16,828 --> 01:32:18,930
We promised to save
whoever took a hit, no matter what.

2106
01:32:19,130 --> 01:32:20,897
- Let's keep our word.
- Then...

2107
01:32:20,898 --> 01:32:21,731
(Genie, holds immunity card)

2108
01:32:21,732 --> 01:32:23,166
This is a tough spot.

2109
01:32:23,701 --> 01:32:26,102
- First off, I have one.
- Who's holding immunity right now?

2110
01:32:26,204 --> 01:32:28,605
- Benjamin and Genie have cards.
- Benjamin and...

2111
01:32:32,009 --> 01:32:34,744
(Whose immunity card will they burn?)

2112
01:32:40,184 --> 01:32:41,484
- Should we step inside...
- Yeah.

2113
01:32:41,485 --> 01:32:43,187
- and talk it through?
- Let's talk inside.

2114
01:32:48,860 --> 01:32:52,229
I had a feeling this might happen.

2115
01:32:54,465 --> 01:32:57,000
Two casualties complicates everything.

2116
01:32:57,634 --> 01:32:59,836
First, I want to clarify...

2117
01:33:00,171 --> 01:33:02,205
what we actually agreed to earlier.

2118
01:33:02,206 --> 01:33:05,175
We only accounted for a single casualty.

2119
01:33:05,176 --> 01:33:07,244
We never planned for two.

2120
01:33:07,847 --> 01:33:09,880
If we truly had a binding agreement,

2121
01:33:09,881 --> 01:33:12,917
one of us would have
to surrender our immunity.

2122
01:33:12,918 --> 01:33:14,952
Did we ever actually set that rule?

2123
01:33:14,953 --> 01:33:16,252
Earlier, all we said was...

2124
01:33:16,253 --> 01:33:20,624
that if we put those four names
on the chopping block...

2125
01:33:20,625 --> 01:33:22,459
and they turned out to be innocent,

2126
01:33:22,460 --> 01:33:24,528
we'd basically be condemning
our own people.

2127
01:33:24,529 --> 01:33:26,663
- So we protect them.
- Exactly.

2128
01:33:26,664 --> 01:33:28,098
- If they take a hit, we revive them.
- Right.

2129
01:33:28,099 --> 01:33:30,500
That was the whole conversation.

2130
01:33:30,501 --> 01:33:33,370
We never agreed
that if bodies started dropping,

2131
01:33:33,371 --> 01:33:36,139
we'd hand over all our immunity cards.

2132
01:33:36,140 --> 01:33:37,507
We never talked about that.

2133
01:33:37,508 --> 01:33:39,977
Not once did I say...

2134
01:33:40,077 --> 01:33:41,811
I'd give mine away.

2135
01:33:42,179 --> 01:33:44,380
Personally,

2136
01:33:44,381 --> 01:33:47,617
given my previous pledges...

2137
01:33:47,618 --> 01:33:49,919
and my track record as daily leader,

2138
01:33:49,920 --> 01:33:51,389
I never made a blanket promise...

2139
01:33:52,057 --> 01:33:54,958
to burn my immunity
on the very first casualty.

2140
01:33:54,959 --> 01:33:57,460
That was never part of today's pledge.

2141
01:34:02,700 --> 01:34:05,135
If this was the expectation all along,

2142
01:34:05,136 --> 01:34:07,337
we should've pooled
our immunity cards up front.

2143
01:34:07,338 --> 01:34:08,338
Why spring this on us now?

2144
01:34:08,339 --> 01:34:10,274
- Doing this out of nowhere...
- I agree, this...

2145
01:34:10,275 --> 01:34:11,708
- doesn't feel right.
- Same here.

2146
01:34:11,709 --> 01:34:14,378
- This is completely wrong.
- I can't get behind this. It's messed up.

2147
01:34:15,446 --> 01:34:17,414
This is human nature for you.

2148
01:34:17,848 --> 01:34:21,516
He promised government safety nets
would keep everyone alive.

2149
01:34:21,517 --> 01:34:23,153
Because we have immunity.

2150
01:34:23,154 --> 01:34:24,989
Except the math doesn't check out.

2151
01:34:25,189 --> 01:34:27,356
If that pledge won her the election,

2152
01:34:27,357 --> 01:34:31,194
she should've secured
all four immunity cards...

2153
01:34:31,195 --> 01:34:33,029
so she could actually deploy them.

2154
01:34:33,030 --> 01:34:36,833
Before writing on that board
and getting this underway,

2155
01:34:36,834 --> 01:34:38,134
she should've locked that down.

2156
01:34:38,135 --> 01:34:40,004
She doesn't even hold the cards.

2157
01:34:40,104 --> 01:34:41,871
Then it's not her power to wield.

2158
01:34:42,139 --> 01:34:44,307
Is there really anything to hesitate over?

2159
01:34:44,308 --> 01:34:46,909
- None at all.
- Look, everyone has their own dilemmas.

2160
01:34:46,910 --> 01:34:48,411
We were aligned from the start.

2161
01:34:48,412 --> 01:34:51,681
We spent all that time deliberating
and settled on that decision.

2162
01:34:52,250 --> 01:34:54,485
Why hold a meeting
if we're going to backtrack now?

2163
01:34:54,952 --> 01:34:56,053
What are we doing here?

2164
01:34:56,220 --> 01:34:58,154
I bet they're hesitating because...

2165
01:34:58,155 --> 01:35:01,991
if they transfer immunity now
and catch a bullet tomorrow,

2166
01:35:01,992 --> 01:35:04,694
they'll feel completely played.

2167
01:35:04,695 --> 01:35:06,562
- Having second thoughts now?
- That's human instinct.

2168
01:35:06,563 --> 01:35:07,630
In that case...

2169
01:35:07,631 --> 01:35:11,167
I wouldn't do it. I really wouldn't.

2170
01:35:11,469 --> 01:35:14,037
We'd basically be sacrificing...

2171
01:35:14,348 --> 01:35:16,149
three lives to prop up one person.

2172
01:35:16,174 --> 01:35:18,009
If we get taken out tomorrow,

2173
01:35:18,010 --> 01:35:20,010
who compensates us?

2174
01:35:20,378 --> 01:35:22,913
I'm skeptical about giving it away.

2175
01:35:23,747 --> 01:35:26,750
(Ideology Code Game: Round Three)

2176
01:35:27,651 --> 01:35:30,052
- Look at the clock.
- At five minutes, one person...

2177
01:35:30,053 --> 01:35:31,822
Judging by how quiet they're being,

2178
01:35:31,847 --> 01:35:34,490
they might just let the casualties
get evicted.

2179
01:35:34,625 --> 01:35:35,992
Six minutes left.

2180
01:35:36,660 --> 01:35:38,794
What do you think we should do, then?

2181
01:35:39,397 --> 01:35:41,565
Instead of just listening to ourselves,

2182
01:35:41,566 --> 01:35:43,433
we should bring in outside perspectives.

2183
01:35:43,434 --> 01:35:45,302
We can't drag everyone into the room.

2184
01:35:45,303 --> 01:35:48,071
Why not talk to the victims directly?

2185
01:35:49,040 --> 01:35:51,109
What would we even ask them?

2186
01:35:51,110 --> 01:35:53,610
They're obviously going
to beg for the cards.

2187
01:35:53,878 --> 01:35:55,045
Would that change anything?

2188
01:35:55,312 --> 01:35:57,346
Should we bring Hippo and Michael in?

2189
01:35:57,347 --> 01:35:59,682
What's the play here, then?
I honestly don't know.

2190
01:36:00,551 --> 01:36:01,450
We have to make a call.

2191
01:36:01,451 --> 01:36:03,520
Talking to them won't solve this.

2192
01:36:04,155 --> 01:36:05,779
They can't bring themselves
to give up the cards.

2193
01:36:05,803 --> 01:36:07,157
- Right.
- They just can't.

2194
01:36:07,458 --> 01:36:09,092
We're out of time.

2195
01:36:09,427 --> 01:36:11,795
There's barely any time left.

2196
01:36:11,796 --> 01:36:17,467
They might genuinely be considering
just letting us get cut.

2197
01:36:17,868 --> 01:36:20,269
Time was slipping away,
but nobody was walking out.

2198
01:36:20,270 --> 01:36:21,838
The clock kept running down.

2199
01:36:21,839 --> 01:36:25,475
This was completely diverging
from the plan.

2200
01:36:25,810 --> 01:36:27,710
Once that timer hits zero,
we're actually gone.

2201
01:36:27,711 --> 01:36:29,412
Reality hit me like a truck.

2202
01:36:29,413 --> 01:36:31,081
Is this really that hard of a choice?

2203
01:36:31,182 --> 01:36:33,449
They weren't facing immediate elimination.

2204
01:36:33,450 --> 01:36:35,619
All they had to do was pass over immunity.

2205
01:36:35,620 --> 01:36:37,320
Is that really so agonizing?

2206
01:36:37,488 --> 01:36:39,689
We'd all been searching for a way
to ensure everyone survived.

2207
01:36:39,690 --> 01:36:42,859
Last night, we even left
the window unlocked...

2208
01:36:42,860 --> 01:36:44,494
just to pull it off.

2209
01:36:44,671 --> 01:36:45,817
(Dark Knight, special forces veteran)

2210
01:36:45,841 --> 01:36:47,206
(Right, equalism,
working-class, conservative)

2211
01:36:47,231 --> 01:36:49,165
Just to protect a single immunity card,

2212
01:36:49,400 --> 01:36:51,968
all the convictions
they had paraded around...

2213
01:36:51,969 --> 01:36:55,472
and every sweet word
about caring for the house...

2214
01:36:55,473 --> 01:36:58,041
instantly revealed itself as an act.

2215
01:36:58,742 --> 01:37:02,612
Instead of calling this
the leader's immunity,

2216
01:37:02,613 --> 01:37:04,247
I'll call it Polar Bear's personal card.

2217
01:37:04,248 --> 01:37:06,438
Still, you need to exercise caution.

2218
01:37:06,462 --> 01:37:07,550
You're the leader now.

2219
01:37:07,551 --> 01:37:09,952
I'm not saying they don't matter.

2220
01:37:09,953 --> 01:37:13,422
If a compelling reason presents itself
and the cause is justified, we use it.

2221
01:37:13,791 --> 01:37:15,967
But promising it blindly
to the very first casualty...

2222
01:37:15,992 --> 01:37:17,493
is way too reckless.

2223
01:37:17,518 --> 01:37:21,721
What if someone indispensable
to the leader takes a hit later on?

2224
01:37:27,338 --> 01:37:30,974
When Michael kept feeling cornered...

2225
01:37:31,209 --> 01:37:32,209
while I held the leadership...

2226
01:37:32,234 --> 01:37:34,476
If we want to save both,
we need to sprint right now.

2227
01:37:34,477 --> 01:37:35,678
Four minutes left.

2228
01:37:35,679 --> 01:37:37,014
- It's three minutes now.
- As leader,

2229
01:37:37,015 --> 01:37:39,615
I personally promised Michael
I'd protect him.

2230
01:37:40,451 --> 01:37:44,320
That's my word, and I have to honor it.

2231
01:37:44,321 --> 01:37:45,522
On top of that, as leader...

2232
01:37:45,523 --> 01:37:49,159
I pledged to do everything possible
to save one more life.

2233
01:37:49,503 --> 01:37:51,638
So when it comes to Michael,

2234
01:37:51,663 --> 01:37:53,062
- I have to stand by it.
- Wait, so you're saying...

2235
01:37:53,063 --> 01:37:55,231
you made a backroom deal?

2236
01:37:55,232 --> 01:37:56,799
What about the three of us?

2237
01:37:56,800 --> 01:38:00,169
None of us ever agreed to that.

2238
01:38:00,170 --> 01:38:01,671
There was never a rule in place.

2239
01:38:02,039 --> 01:38:04,207
I'll run up and grab mine first.

2240
01:38:04,575 --> 01:38:06,709
We're running out of time,
and it's upstairs.

2241
01:38:08,780 --> 01:38:10,914
I could tell they were terrified...

2242
01:38:10,939 --> 01:38:14,184
of exposing their refusal
to part with immunity.

2243
01:38:14,185 --> 01:38:16,119
It was written all over their faces.

2244
01:38:16,120 --> 01:38:20,857
Even when I made the executive call
to use the leader's card on Michael,

2245
01:38:20,858 --> 01:38:23,026
they pushed back fiercely.

2246
01:38:23,027 --> 01:38:26,263
They were petrified
that if one person stepped up with a card,

2247
01:38:26,288 --> 01:38:28,866
the rest would look like monsters
for holding onto theirs.

2248
01:38:29,233 --> 01:38:31,801
Even with Polar Bear's card, though...

2249
01:38:31,802 --> 01:38:33,769
We really need to think this through.

2250
01:38:33,770 --> 01:38:35,104
Because if we play it this way,

2251
01:38:35,339 --> 01:38:37,974
- I'd rather she didn't.
- it paints this in black and white.

2252
01:38:37,975 --> 01:38:39,810
This is the first time
anyone is deploying immunity.

2253
01:38:39,977 --> 01:38:41,144
- But Polar Bear,
- Look...

2254
01:38:41,612 --> 01:38:44,380
Go Ae Shin just raised a valid concern.

2255
01:38:44,515 --> 01:38:47,750
This could starkly frame us
into good versus evil.

2256
01:38:47,885 --> 01:38:48,751
Good versus evil?

2257
01:38:48,752 --> 01:38:50,854
It sets up a narrative...

2258
01:38:50,855 --> 01:38:52,889
- of heroes and villains.
- Let me explain.

2259
01:38:53,757 --> 01:38:55,424
At this rate, we're not saving anyone.

2260
01:38:55,726 --> 01:38:57,260
We have literally one minute left.

2261
01:38:58,762 --> 01:39:00,698
Instead of framing this
as good versus evil,

2262
01:39:00,798 --> 01:39:03,833
just look at it
as Polar Bear's personal card.

2263
01:39:03,934 --> 01:39:04,867
Or...

2264
01:39:04,868 --> 01:39:07,837
can we just announce
we're burning one out of the four?

2265
01:39:07,838 --> 01:39:09,138
(Donor's anonymity requested)

2266
01:39:09,873 --> 01:39:10,739
Fine.

2267
01:39:10,874 --> 01:39:13,809
Out of the four immunity cards,

2268
01:39:13,810 --> 01:39:17,413
we've agreed to deploy just one.

2269
01:39:21,619 --> 01:39:23,053
We're down to the wire.

2270
01:39:23,654 --> 01:39:25,855
Run if you're saving them!
One minute, ten seconds left!

2271
01:39:32,663 --> 01:39:33,697
Time is almost up.

2272
01:39:34,965 --> 01:39:35,932
Let's go.

2273
01:39:35,933 --> 01:39:37,900
As for what comes next,

2274
01:39:37,901 --> 01:39:39,735
- We take it case by case.
- I'll explain everything later.

2275
01:39:39,736 --> 01:39:41,304
Understood. Let's hear
what the leader has to say.

2276
01:39:41,305 --> 01:39:42,772
(Ideology Code Game)

2277
01:40:05,229 --> 01:40:06,062
Good grief.

2278
01:40:10,768 --> 01:40:12,969
The other three definitely
aren't stepping up, right?

2279
01:40:12,970 --> 01:40:14,704
When she gets back,
we'll explain it together.

2280
01:40:14,705 --> 01:40:17,374
Whether you explain it or not,
the clock is running out.

2281
01:40:17,375 --> 01:40:18,308
Are you sure about this?

2282
01:40:20,477 --> 01:40:23,980
(Ideology Code Game: Round Three)

2283
01:40:25,549 --> 01:40:26,949
Take a good look in the mirror.

2284
01:40:26,950 --> 01:40:28,519
Is the spy really the problem...

2285
01:40:29,486 --> 01:40:31,021
or is it your own cowardice?

2286
01:40:32,756 --> 01:40:35,291
Maybe in some sense,
every single one of us is a spy.

2287
01:40:44,501 --> 01:40:46,802
Polar Bear failed
to hold the room together.

2288
01:40:46,904 --> 01:40:50,206
She couldn't even consolidate power.

2289
01:40:50,207 --> 01:40:51,162
Total inexperience,

2290
01:40:51,186 --> 01:40:52,742
the textbook definition
of ineffective leadership.

2291
01:40:53,544 --> 01:40:56,579
They chose to save only one person,
and they picked Michael?

2292
01:40:56,580 --> 01:40:58,857
The leader literally campaigned
on protecting the vulnerable.

2293
01:40:58,882 --> 01:41:00,884
By every objective metric,

2294
01:41:00,885 --> 01:41:02,694
wasn't Hippo the one
who needed protection?

2295
01:41:02,719 --> 01:41:03,552
(Banu, top student)

2296
01:41:03,553 --> 01:41:05,287
I don't believe society will keep me safe.

2297
01:41:05,288 --> 01:41:06,789
Anxiety started creeping in.

2298
01:41:08,792 --> 01:41:12,061
It felt like we'd been branded
as cold-blooded criminals.

2299
01:41:12,096 --> 01:41:14,297
If anyone was the real villain,

2300
01:41:14,298 --> 01:41:16,966
it was whoever went around
assassinating people with ideology checks.

2301
01:41:16,967 --> 01:41:18,334
They were the guilty ones.

2302
01:41:18,335 --> 01:41:20,770
Yet somehow, those of us...

2303
01:41:20,771 --> 01:41:23,206
who chose to hold onto our immunity
were made to feel guilty.

2304
01:41:23,207 --> 01:41:24,908
That really weighed on my conscience.

2305
01:41:25,409 --> 01:41:27,043
It was just...

2306
01:41:27,044 --> 01:41:29,678
(Genie, elite corporate employee)

2307
01:41:29,679 --> 01:41:31,447
To be fair, I...

2308
01:41:31,448 --> 01:41:33,483
also knew Hippo's code.

2309
01:41:33,484 --> 01:41:35,718
Yet I never pulled the trigger.

2310
01:41:35,886 --> 01:41:37,820
In my own way, back then,

2311
01:41:38,055 --> 01:41:40,490
I chose to spare her.

2312
01:41:40,691 --> 01:41:44,627
And now, simply because I kept
my immunity card...

2313
01:41:44,628 --> 01:41:46,996
I don't know. It's a complicated feeling.

2314
01:41:47,698 --> 01:41:51,768
I'm honestly stunned
that Polar Bear opted to save Michael.

2315
01:41:52,002 --> 01:41:53,036
That's just my honest reaction.

2316
01:41:53,037 --> 01:41:55,137
Then again, she gave her word,
so she had to follow through.

2317
01:41:55,606 --> 01:41:57,107
Everyone sees things
through their own lens.

2318
01:41:57,274 --> 01:41:58,874
She might believe
she's safe from elimination.

2319
01:41:58,875 --> 01:42:00,210
Still, sitting around debating...

2320
01:42:00,235 --> 01:42:03,379
whether I should surrender my card
is completely absurd.

2321
01:42:03,380 --> 01:42:05,215
It's mine.

2322
01:42:05,216 --> 01:42:07,516
If they wanted to strip it away,
put a system in place...

2323
01:42:07,985 --> 01:42:08,985
or use raw leverage.

2324
01:42:08,986 --> 01:42:11,487
Otherwise, they're just relying
on blind charity.

2325
01:42:11,488 --> 01:42:14,157
I'm the spy. Why would I show charity?

2326
01:42:14,158 --> 01:42:16,626
The rest of them are thinking
the exact same thing anyway.

2327
01:42:16,627 --> 01:42:17,660
"I'm surviving this."

2328
01:42:17,661 --> 01:42:19,495
They should've codified a rule
from day one.

2329
01:42:19,496 --> 01:42:22,632
That would've made things
much more complicated.

2330
01:42:31,742 --> 01:42:32,709
I see how it is.

2331
01:42:36,880 --> 01:42:39,615
Nothing could illustrate the reality
more clearly.

2332
01:42:40,184 --> 01:42:41,518
Words are completely meaningless.

2333
01:42:42,252 --> 01:42:44,086
The immunity card...

2334
01:42:44,855 --> 01:42:46,522
I never dreamed they wouldn't use it.

2335
01:42:46,523 --> 01:42:49,292
It makes them look utterly spineless.

2336
01:42:49,293 --> 01:42:53,563
I didn't think they'd backtrack
so shamelessly.

2337
01:42:53,564 --> 01:42:55,465
Even during her speech that day,

2338
01:42:55,466 --> 01:42:57,634
she swore to protect
as many people as possible.

2339
01:42:57,901 --> 01:43:01,403
Does politics always do a complete 180...

2340
01:43:01,505 --> 01:43:04,507
the second the campaign ends
and power takes over?

2341
01:43:04,708 --> 01:43:06,343
Is that just the nature of politics?

2342
01:43:10,747 --> 01:43:12,981
I'd like to transfer immunity.

2343
01:43:13,751 --> 01:43:16,585
Processing immunity transfer.

2344
01:43:16,687 --> 01:43:18,388
Transferring to Michael.

2345
01:43:19,756 --> 01:43:21,824
Polar Bear's immunity...

2346
01:43:22,092 --> 01:43:24,493
has been applied to Michael.

2347
01:43:26,263 --> 01:43:29,498
The Code Deduction Game has ended.

2348
01:43:29,800 --> 01:43:32,402
Victim Hippo,

2349
01:43:32,736 --> 01:43:36,939
please exit the Community House
immediately.

2350
01:43:37,441 --> 01:43:40,777
(Hippo becomes the first evictee.)

2351
01:43:52,823 --> 01:43:55,525
We should at least say goodbye
before she leaves.

2352
01:43:55,760 --> 01:43:56,626
You fought hard.

2353
01:44:06,770 --> 01:44:09,572
To be honest,

2354
01:44:10,173 --> 01:44:12,074
before I turned into someone like that,

2355
01:44:14,077 --> 01:44:15,712
I'm almost glad I got eliminated.

2356
01:44:16,747 --> 01:44:17,880
Words are cheap.

2357
01:44:17,881 --> 01:44:19,449
(Hippo, writer, former feminism activist)

2358
01:44:19,450 --> 01:44:24,153
Words tell you absolutely nothing
about a person's true character.

2359
01:44:24,288 --> 01:44:28,424
That realization hit me
with immense weight.

2360
01:44:28,859 --> 01:44:34,063
We traded so many beautiful,
morally righteous speeches.

2361
01:44:34,331 --> 01:44:36,933
Yet isn't this the rawest truth of all?

2362
01:44:37,568 --> 01:44:39,335
Not just for me, but going forward,

2363
01:44:39,336 --> 01:44:41,437
they'll be confronted
with countless brutal choices.

2364
01:44:41,438 --> 01:44:43,907
Those decisions will reveal
who they truly are.

2365
01:44:47,077 --> 01:44:49,612
(12 Hippo)

2366
01:44:50,681 --> 01:44:52,848
I was terrified to join this show.

2367
01:44:52,849 --> 01:44:55,684
Mainly because my political stance...

2368
01:44:55,685 --> 01:44:57,486
isn't anywhere near moderate.

2369
01:44:58,188 --> 01:44:59,555
As my scores clearly showed.

2370
01:45:00,190 --> 01:45:03,025
Putting that on display
for the entire country...

2371
01:45:03,393 --> 01:45:05,794
took serious courage.

2372
01:45:05,795 --> 01:45:07,396
People will have endless opinions.

2373
01:45:07,397 --> 01:45:09,465
About me, and about this show.

2374
01:45:09,466 --> 01:45:12,801
Yet whatever judgments they pass,

2375
01:45:12,802 --> 01:45:15,270
I came to realize
it was never truly about me.

2376
01:45:15,772 --> 01:45:17,785
They were just projecting
their own baggage...

2377
01:45:17,809 --> 01:45:19,441
onto whatever they wanted to see.

2378
01:45:19,743 --> 01:45:22,411
All I could do was stay true to myself.

2379
01:45:22,979 --> 01:45:24,981
I believe The Community is a space...

2380
01:45:24,982 --> 01:45:27,884
where people discover
what they need to face.

2381
01:45:27,885 --> 01:45:29,385
That goes for the cast,

2382
01:45:29,620 --> 01:45:32,222
and hopefully for the viewers
watching at home as well.

2383
01:45:40,797 --> 01:45:43,732
I want to express just how sorry I am...

2384
01:45:44,267 --> 01:45:47,269
that we had to say goodbye...

2385
01:45:48,338 --> 01:45:49,338
to one of our own.

2386
01:45:50,574 --> 01:45:52,275
Why is everyone dead silent?

2387
01:45:53,143 --> 01:45:56,078
You all talked such a big game
during the meetings.

2388
01:45:57,247 --> 01:45:59,615
You huddled inside for over ten minutes,

2389
01:46:00,149 --> 01:46:02,084
running out the clock
until the final second.

2390
01:46:02,085 --> 01:46:04,420
What took you so long to say?

2391
01:46:05,122 --> 01:46:07,023
Pretentious hypocrites putting on a show.

2392
01:46:07,024 --> 01:46:08,157
They're all talk.

2393
01:46:08,158 --> 01:46:09,826
How can people be so pathetic?

2394
01:46:10,127 --> 01:46:13,763
We will now reveal
the ideology codes for all residents.

2395
01:46:13,764 --> 01:46:15,666
Why reveal them now? This is unbearable.
